"strategy","subs":[{"id":"cmq-strategy","lesson":"/lessons.html","lessonName":"Browse lessons","name":"II. Strategic Plan Development & Deployment","w":23}],"weight":23},{"domain":"management","subs":[{"id":"cmq-management","lesson":"/lessons.html","lessonName":"Browse lessons","name":"III. Management Elements & Methods","w":26}],"weight":26},{"domain":"tools","subs":[{"id":"cmq-tools","lesson":"/lessons.html","lessonName":"Browse lessons","name":"IV. Quality Management Tools","w":31}],"weight":31},{"domain":"customer","subs":[{"id":"cmq-customer","lesson":"/lessons.html","lessonName":"Browse lessons","name":"V. Customer-Focused Organizations","w":22}],"weight":22},{"domain":"supply","subs":[{"id":"cmq-supply","lesson":"/lessons.html","lessonName":"Browse lessons","name":"VI. Supply Chain Management","w":19}],"weight":19},{"domain":"training","subs":[{"id":"cmq-training","lesson":"/lessons.html","lessonName":"Browse lessons","name":"VII. Training & Development","w":16}],"weight":16}],"fullExamQuestionsBySet":{},"gradingPolicyVersion":"single-select-v1","masteryPolicyVersion":"baseline-confidence-v1","minutes":270,"questions":150,"siteTargetBps":7000,"timingPolicyVersion":"site-proportional-v1","title":"Manager of Quality — Final Exam Simulation"},"configVersion":"8ea161b08049f1c907c9adf8da501599804e2b4a8ec3e661e6dcc5663406d2b0","contents":{"cmq:set-1:source-1":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"Tell the team to have a nonbinding vote before beginning a discussion, which will make each person''s view apparent.\",\"Ask the team to fill out a questionnaire rating themselves on effective group process.\",\"Tell the quiet members they need to speak out.\",\"Ask what the impact will be on the team if they don''t adequately discuss issues.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":1,\"stem\":\"A facilitator notices that the team jumps to conclusions after only one or two members have stated their opinion. The facilitator should:\",\"sub\":\"cmq-lead\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the leadership, organizational-culture, ethics, or change-management principle tested by the scenario. <b>D. Ask what the impact will be on the team if they don''t adequately discuss issues.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["Tell the team to have a nonbinding vote before beginning a discussion, which will make each person''s view apparent.","Ask the team to fill out a questionnaire rating themselves on effective group process.","Tell the quiet members they need to speak out.","Ask what the impact will be on the team if they don''t adequately discuss issues."],"sourceQuestion":1,"stem":"A facilitator notices that the team jumps to conclusions after only one or two members have stated their opinion. The facilitator should:","sub":"cmq-lead","why":"This response best applies the leadership, organizational-culture, ethics, or change-management principle tested by the scenario. <b>D. Ask what the impact will be on the team if they don''t adequately discuss issues.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 1.</span>"},"revision":"689a630661b12416a4edfaeb6c9ea8368ac4093417116bae9c9232506960347f"},"cmq:set-1:source-10":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"Advertising agencies.\",\"Competitors.\",\"Stakeholders.\",\"Public relations advisers.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":10,\"stem\":\"During the development of company strategy, input should be sought from:\",\"sub\":\"cmq-strategy\",\"why\":\"This response best aligns the decision with sound strategic planning, environmental analysis, deployment, and measurement. <b>C. Stakeholders.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 10.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["Advertising agencies.","Competitors.","Stakeholders.","Public relations advisers."],"sourceQuestion":10,"stem":"During the development of company strategy, input should be sought from:","sub":"cmq-strategy","why":"This response best aligns the decision with sound strategic planning, environmental analysis, deployment, and measurement. <b>C. Stakeholders.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 10.</span>"},"revision":"d2ee685eca177fcc4ad1eca60419a7192bc2d72e07b2566672aa96f23c0b45e8"},"cmq:set-1:source-100":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"III only\",\"II and III only\",\"II, III, and IV only\",\"I, II, III, and IV\"],\"sourceQuestion\":100,\"stem\":\"For a bookseller that sells entirely through a Web site, managing the diversity of customers would entail which of the following? I. Adopting lean techniques to reduce cycle time II. Continually developing new service features to take the place of services that have become \\\"must haves\\\" III. Responding to the needs of a diverse customer base IV. Understanding and working closely with multiple publishers\",\"sub\":\"cmq-customer\",\"why\":\"Managing customer diversity means responding to differing customer needs and continuing to differentiate services as expectations evolve. Lean cycle-time work and publisher management may support operations, but they do not directly manage customer diversity. <b>B. II and III only</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 100; answer corrected for student use.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["III only","II and III only","II, III, and IV only","I, II, III, and IV"],"sourceQuestion":100,"stem":"For a bookseller that sells entirely through a Web site, managing the diversity of customers would entail which of the following? I. Adopting lean techniques to reduce cycle time II. Continually developing new service features to take the place of services that have become \"must haves\" III. Responding to the needs of a diverse customer base IV. Understanding and working closely with multiple publishers","sub":"cmq-customer","why":"Managing customer diversity means responding to differing customer needs and continuing to differentiate services as expectations evolve. Lean cycle-time work and publisher management may support operations, but they do not directly manage customer diversity. <b>B. II and III only</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 100; answer corrected for student use.</span>"},"revision":"9ee89d20cdddf1a8677200eea1a5c8eb7c1593a79d96f4b68a90733ccac613c7"},"cmq:set-1:source-101":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"Quality award winner.\",\"Financial stability of supplier.\",\"Capability to meet current and future demands.\",\"Supplier''s track record for on-time delivery and incoming quality.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":101,\"stem\":\"Typical factors chosen as criteria for supplier selection would include all but:\",\"sub\":\"cmq-supply\",\"why\":\"This response best supports effective supplier selection, performance, procurement, partnership, or logistics management. <b>A. Quality award winner.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 101.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["Quality award winner.","Financial stability of supplier.","Capability to meet current and future demands.","Supplier''s track record for on-time delivery and incoming quality."],"sourceQuestion":101,"stem":"Typical factors chosen as criteria for supplier selection would include all but:","sub":"cmq-supply","why":"This response best supports effective supplier selection, performance, procurement, partnership, or logistics management. <b>A. Quality award winner.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 101.</span>"},"revision":"3bff11156a2d3f8c602d3c3a7b4e0373c977cc67e2ab28ddcf82aadffe51ceed"},"cmq:set-1:source-102":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"I and III only\",\"I and II only\",\"I, II, and III only\",\"I, II, III, and IV\"],\"sourceQuestion\":102,\"stem\":\"A condition under which a supplier appearing on the customer''s \\\"OK to buy from\\\" list would not be issued an order would be: I. Item needed is not available from any of OK''d suppliers. II. Supplier''s quality rating has dropped below acceptable standards on last two shipments. III. OK''d supplier does not have the capacity to fulfill the customer''s demands for the item needed. IV. One or more factors from the selection criteria will not now be met by the supplier.\",\"sub\":\"cmq-supply\",\"why\":\"This response best supports effective supplier selection, performance, procurement, partnership, or logistics management. <b>D. I, II, III, and IV</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 102.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["I and III only","I and II only","I, II, and III only","I, II, III, and IV"],"sourceQuestion":102,"stem":"A condition under which a supplier appearing on the customer''s \"OK to buy from\" list would not be issued an order would be: I. Item needed is not available from any of OK''d suppliers. II. Supplier''s quality rating has dropped below acceptable standards on last two shipments. III. OK''d supplier does not have the capacity to fulfill the customer''s demands for the item needed. IV. One or more factors from the selection criteria will not now be met by the supplier.","sub":"cmq-supply","why":"This response best supports effective supplier selection, performance, procurement, partnership, or logistics management. <b>D. I, II, III, and IV</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 102.</span>"},"revision":"9bed13b4c25c21639a7f3b3c05041ebee3cd59f27c233f5506291fe862fe8cf0"},"cmq:set-1:source-103":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"II, III, and IV only\",\"III and IV only\",\"I, II, and III only\",\"I, II, III, and IV\"],\"sourceQuestion\":103,\"stem\":\"In medical device manufacturing and in pharmaceutical production, strict traceability is mandated by regu