ional results</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 120.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["Improved technological capabilities","Improved human resource capabilities","Improved employee satisfaction","Improved operational results"],"sourceQuestion":120,"stem":"Which of the following is the primary purpose of training?","sub":"cmq-training","why":"This response best applies training-needs, adult-learning, delivery, or evaluation principles. <b>D. Improved operational results</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 120.</span>"},"revision":"d19384a36cfb1142a1ac317575c91fc38bc4e6aceffc539abcd7bb653879e620"},"cmq:set-1:source-121":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"A new law requires that training be done\",\"A continual stream of terminations and new hires is occurring\",\"A cell structure is being created and all employees within each cell must be able to do any task within the cell\",\"A performance gap is caused solely by unavailable equipment, and employees already demonstrate the required skills\"],\"sourceQuestion\":121,\"stem\":\"Training appears to be needed in all but one of the following situations. Which one?\",\"sub\":\"cmq-training\",\"why\":\"Training cannot correct a performance gap caused solely by unavailable equipment when employees already have the required knowledge and skills. The other situations introduce a legal, onboarding, or cross-training requirement. <b>D. A performance gap is caused solely by unavailable equipment, and employees already demonstrate the required skills</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 121; ambiguous choice repaired for student use.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["A new law requires that training be done","A continual stream of terminations and new hires is occurring","A cell structure is being created and all employees within each cell must be able to do an