dy Guide CMQ-OE, Question 122.</span>"},"revision":"dc2dabcf846fc332f3a717a5dcf613c1d84dc147d25e345765830db719daa940"},"cmq:set-1:source-123":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"Critical incident analysis\",\"Focus group\",\"Task analysis\",\"Annual budget variance analysis\"],\"sourceQuestion\":123,\"stem\":\"All except one of the following is a technique used in assessing training needs. Which one is not?\",\"sub\":\"cmq-training\",\"why\":\"Critical incidents, focus groups, and task analysis can identify knowledge or skill gaps. Annual budget variance analysis is a financial-control technique, not a training-needs assessment method. <b>D. Annual budget variance analysis</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 123; ambiguous choice repaired for student use.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["Critical incident analysis","Focus group","Task analysis","Annual budget variance analysis"],"sourceQuestion":123,"stem":"All except one of the following is a technique used in assessing training needs. Which one is not?","sub":"cmq-training","why":"Critical incidents, focus groups, and task analysis can identify knowledge or skill gaps. Annual budget variance analysis is a financial-control technique, not a training-needs assessment method. <b>D. Annual budget variance analysis</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 123; ambiguous choice repaired for student use.</span>"},"revision":"71d833ff6d7ebb6887b5d8175b2528a4b95eda0391c1977516b13d5bce9a45c3"},"cmq:set-1:source-124":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"Learner-controlled instruction\",\"Classroom instruction\",\"Case studies\",\"Coaching\"],\"sourceQuestion\":124,\"stem\":\"Which of the following training delivery methods would be most effective in a situation with large employee populations, multiple sites needing concurrent delivery, and high turnover rates that require continuous training?\",\"sub\":\