ery, or evaluation principles. <b>D. A signal light indicating that an error has occurred</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 128.</span>"},"revision":"08b77f1bf3d84cdec124287d7b24a2fd6b586021b8d55c94fb9039bcc3c3605a"},"cmq:set-1:source-129":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"I, II, III, IV\",\"II, IV, III, I\",\"II, I, III, IV\",\"IV, III, I, II\"],\"sourceQuestion\":129,\"stem\":\"Which sequence demonstrates the lowest-to-highest order for evaluating training effectiveness? I. What changes in behavior resulted? (Behavior); II. What tangible results did the program produce? (Results); III. What principles, facts, or techniques were learned? (Learning); IV. How well did attendees like the program? (Reaction).\",\"sub\":\"cmq-training\",\"why\":\"This response best applies training-needs, adult-learning, delivery, or evaluation principles. <b>D. IV, III, I, II</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 129.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["I, II, III, IV","II, IV, III, I","II, I, III, IV","IV, III, I, II"],"sourceQuestion":129,"stem":"Which sequence demonstrates the lowest-to-highest order for evaluating training effectiveness? I. What changes in behavior resulted? (Behavior); II. What tangible results did the program produce? (Results); III. What principles, facts, or techniques were learned? (Learning); IV. How well did attendees like the program? (Reaction).","sub":"cmq-training","why":"This response best applies training-needs, adult-learning, delivery, or evaluation principles. <b>D. IV, III, I, II</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 129.</span>"},"revision":"304cbed16db9823cea9ad695a18d95b279068c36286102f5141be2af9fb8f217"},"cmq:set-1:source-13":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"Institute and enforce a quality policy across all organizational functions.\",\"Lead the implementation of an ISO 9001 QM