rs\"],\"sourceQuestion\":141,\"stem\":\"A chairperson may be a leader and/or manager, depending much upon the influence he or she may have on an organization and the decision authority granted. There are many roles a manager may perform. As an architect he/she:\",\"sub\":\"cmq-lead\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the leadership, organizational-culture, ethics, or change-management principle tested by the scenario. <b>B. Builds an enterprise structure that supports the strategic goals and objectives</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 141.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["Organizes, people, ideas and things to achieve the enterprise''s objectives","Builds an enterprise structure that supports the strategic goals and objectives","Embraces the principles, morals, and norms of the society in which organization impacts","Imparts knowledge and teaches skills to others"],"sourceQuestion":141,"stem":"A chairperson may be a leader and/or manager, depending much upon the influence he or she may have on an organization and the decision authority granted. There are many roles a manager may perform. As an architect he/she:","sub":"cmq-lead","why":"This response best applies the leadership, organizational-culture, ethics, or change-management principle tested by the scenario. <b>B. Builds an enterprise structure that supports the strategic goals and objectives</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 141.</span>"},"revision":"204143b6f2deeb5cb0471efe40e1f9f8665fb1f3ca68971193494850e7660da2"},"cmq:set-1:source-142":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"The task of economic performance\",\"The task to make work productive and worker achieving\",\"The task to managing the social impacts and social responsibilities of the enterprise\",\"The task of managing within the dimension of budget\"],\"sourceQuestion\":142,\"stem\":\"Drucker identifies four tasks of management Excluding:\",\"sub\":\"cmq-lead\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the leadership, organizational-culture, ethics, or change-management principle tested by the scenario. <b>D. The task of managing within the dimension of budget</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 142.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["The task of economic performance","The task to make work productive and worker achieving","The task to managing the social impacts and social responsibilities of the enterprise","The task of managing within the dimension of budget"],"sourceQuestion":142,"stem":"Drucker identifies four tasks of management Excluding:","sub":"cmq-lead","why":"This response best applies the leadership, organizational-culture, ethics, or change-management principle tested by the scenario. <b>D. The task of managing within the dimension of budget</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 142.</span>"},"revision":"97825788e900a0908fda62802069c70468e8c867cff5344b036cee3893223503"},"cmq:set-1:source-143":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"Change agent\",\"Mentor\",\"Ethicist\",\"Business Generator\"],\"sourceQuestion\":143,\"stem\":\"Is a person from outside the organization who has been hired to advise and help facilitate the change process. He/she has greater degree of freedom and should be better able to access activities and provide honest feedback.\",\"sub\":\"cmq-lead\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the leadership, organizational-culture, ethics, or change-management principle tested by the scenario. <b>A. Change agent</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 143.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["Change agent","Mentor","Ethicist","Business Generator"],"sourceQuestion":143,"stem":"Is a person from outside the organization who has been hired to advise and help facilitate the change process. He/she has greater degree of freedom and should be better able to access activities and provide honest feedback.","sub":"cmq-lead","why":"This response best applies the leadership, organizational-culture, ethics, or change-management principle tested by the scenario. <b>A. Change agent</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 143.</span>"},"revision":"b7b9b5fbf8b95898e8ca5bc01f113f7446dedaffbf53e7cd7661a74af41264e6"},"cmq:set-1:source-144":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"To ensure the strategic and operational plans clearly indicate the priorities and strategies for the organization\",\"To communicate, communicate, and communicate!\",\"To ensure that authority levels are clearly spelled out for typical situations\",\"To have employees go outside the organizational walls\"],\"sourceQuestion\":144,\"stem\":\"All organizations have limited resources and opportunities, and must allocate them so as to best accomplish the mission with high efficiency. A possible solution is:\",\"sub\":\"cmq-lead\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the leadership, organizational-culture, ethics, or change-management principle tested by the scenario. <b>A. To ensure the strategic and operational plans clearly indicate the priorities and strategies for the organization</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 144.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["To ensure the strategic and operational plans clearly indicate the priorities and strategies for the organization","To communicate, communicate, and communicate!","To ensure that authority levels are clearly spelled out for typical situations","To have employees go outside the organizational walls"],"sourceQuestion":144,"stem":"All organizations have limited resources and opportunities, and must allocate them so as to best accomplish the mission with high efficiency. A possible solution is:","sub":"cmq-lead","why":"This response best applies the leadership, organizational-culture, ethics, or change-management principle tested by the scenario. <b>A. To ensure the strategic and operational plans clearly indicate the priorities and strategies for the organization</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 144.</span>"},"revision":"46fb8657d74ba17c5557e4091c5cfdde6485a644e2aef890c9427fcda1a2a9f4"},"cmq:set-1:source-145":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"Gantt chart\",\"PERT chart\",\"A force-field analysis\",\"None of these\"],\"sourceQuestion\":145,\"stem\":\"Managing change is particularly complex because much of what must be changed consists of intangibles such as beliefs, behaviors, and policies. These constraints are more difficult to identify. Which tool can help?\",\"sub\":\"cmq-lead\",\"why\":\"Force-field analysis makes the intangible forces supporting and resisting a proposed change explicit so they can be evaluated and addressed. Gantt and PERT charts are scheduling tools. <b>C. A force-field analysis</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 145.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["Gantt chart","PERT chart","A force-field analysis","None of these"],"sourceQuestion":145,"stem":"Managing change is particularly complex because much of what must be changed consists of intangibles such as beliefs, behaviors, and policies. These constraints are more difficult to identify. Which tool can help?","sub":"cmq-lead","why":"Force-field analysis makes the intangible forces supporting and resisting a proposed change explicit so they can be evaluated and addressed. Gantt and PERT charts are scheduling tools. <b>C. A force-field analysis</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 145.</span>"},"revision":"00b48052e4b85a9862c8e12ef5157ef5e49e3b2d350c60506a853b936a23216d"},"cmq:set-1:source-146":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"Understand the emotional impact of change\",\"Understand the impact of change to intellectual property\",\"Be consistent in responding to resistance\",\"Be flexible, be patient and be supportive\"],\"sourceQuestion\":146,\"stem\":\"A modification of Lewin''s unfreezing-moving- refreezing model may provide support for change. According to this model there are following ways to reduce change resistance Except:\",\"sub\":\"cmq-lead\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the leadership, organizational-culture, ethics, or change-management principle tested by the scenario. <b>B. Understand the impact of change to intellectual property</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 146.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["Understand the emotional impact of change","Understand the impact of change to intellectual property","Be consistent in responding to resistance","Be flexible, be patient and be supportive"],"sourceQuestion":146,"stem":"A modification of Lewin''s unfreezing-moving- refreezing model may provide support for change. According to this model there are following ways to reduce change resistance Except:","sub":"cmq-lead","why":"This response best applies the leadership, organizational-culture, ethics, or change-management principle tested by the scenario. <b>B. Understand the impact of change to intellectual property</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 146.</span>"},"revision":"1aa3574758d2a6d4a5e0ed7685f3a5c9b04f4c63e806c0ed946d989d3d67b701"},"cmq:set-1:source-147":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"I and III\",\"II and IV\",\"I, II, and IV\",\"I, II, III, and IV\"],\"sourceQuestion\":147,\"stem\":\"The decision-making authority delegated to lower management levels depends on: I. The situation II. The extent of centralization or decentralization III. Which people in the organization have the best information IV. The complexity of the environment in which the organization functions\",\"sub\":\"cmq-lead\",\"why\":\"This response be