I, and IV</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 29.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["I, III, and IV only","I and III only","I, II, III, and IV","I only"],"sourceQuestion":29,"stem":"Assessing and identifying exposure to risks should: I. Be done prior to investing in a major capital expenditure. II. Be a continual process. III. Be undertaken as part of the feasibility analysis prior to purchasing another business. IV. Include financial, physical, safety, security, health, product liability, and proprietary information risk exposures.","sub":"cmq-management","why":"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>C. I, II, III, and IV</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 29.</span>"},"revision":"89d404a8c71e7de167ad4f641e01253a612e43d958c2011867270336c36db2d4"},"cmq:set-1:source-3":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"Decline, since the team needs to own the process.\",\"Attend with a clear vision of the importance of the project.\",\"Try to identify resisting forces before attending the meeting.\",\"Attend and communicate a sense of urgency.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":3,\"stem\":\"A team is frustrated by the difficulty of the project on which they''re working, and has asked the sponsor to attend their next meeting. The sponsor should:\",\"sub\":\"cmq-management\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>B. Attend with a clear vision of the importance of the project.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 3.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["Decline, since the team needs to own the process.","Attend with a clear vision of the importance of the project.","Try to identify resisting forces before attending the meeting.","Attend and communicate a sense of urgency."],"sourceQuestion":3,"stem":"A team is frustrated by the difficulty of the project on which they''re working, and has asked the sponsor to attend their next meeting. The sponsor should:","sub":"cmq-management","why":"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>B. Attend with a clear vision of the importance of the project.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 3.</span>"},"revision":"35871d1f955b85cd8c08b5b9750563f793bc81b3994c43e253170c3f6a452a74"},"cmq:set-1:source-30":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"I, II, III, and IV\",\"I only\",\"II, III, and IV only\",\"I and II only\"],\"sourceQuestion\":30,\"stem\":\"Which of the following are methods for mitigating risks? I. Eliminate the condition that may cause a loss to occur II. Establish contingency plans III. Obtain insurance to cover some of the potential risk IV. Self-insure\",\"sub\":\"cmq-management\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>A. I, II, III, and IV</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 30.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["I, II, III, and IV","I only","II, III, and IV only","I and II only"],"sourceQuestion":30,"stem":"Which of the following are methods for mitigating risks? I. Eliminate the condition that may cause a loss to occur II. Establish contingency plans III. Obtain insurance to cover some of the potential risk IV. Self-insure","sub":"cmq-management","why":"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>A. I, II, III, and IV</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 30.</span>"},"revision":"8686be717b011a925c22e385255e44ce92cf5d937786af3c669bfea969eea5c1"},"cmq:set-1:source-31":{"canonicalContent":"{\"ans