\",\"sub\":\"cmq-management\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>C. Performance reviews.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 32.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["Employee suggestion boxes.","Quality circles.","Performance reviews.","Employee satisfaction surveys."],"sourceQuestion":32,"stem":"Bottom-to-top communication techniques include all the following except:","sub":"cmq-management","why":"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>C. Performance reviews.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 32.</span>"},"revision":"611e132c12b956d097c36f9564826bf3eeb8960a8a76882c29539808a790288d"},"cmq:set-1:source-33":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"Communication is constrained by chain of command.\",\"Messages are distorted many times by different frames of reference.\",\"Competitive opportunities might be missed because of time delays.\",\"Different functional departments communicate at a different pace.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":33,\"stem\":\"Which of the following is not generally a characteristic of communication in hierarchical organizations?\",\"sub\":\"cmq-management\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>D. Different functional departments communicate at a different pace.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 33.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["Communication is constrained by chain of command.","Messages are distorted many times by different frames of reference.","Competitive opportunities might be missed because of time delays.","Different functional departments communicate at a different pace."],"sourceQuestion":33,"stem":"Which of the following is not generally a characteristic of communication in hierarchical organizations?","sub":"cmq-management","why":"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>D. Different functional departments communicate at a different pace.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 33.</span>"},"revision":"5a72b81473c33094f55ad3b5c7d3b575a063b6cf3ce88f14714113d838481796"},"cmq:set-1:source-34":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"Body language and voice convey the same message.\",\"Use open-ended and closed questions at appropriate times.\",\"Since the brain works much faster than speaking, use the time while another person is speaking to plan your next comment or question.\",\"Use a paraphrasing technique to clarify your understanding of what was said.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":34,\"stem\":\"All but one of the following represents good communicating skill. Which one does not?\",\"sub\":\"cmq-management\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>C. Since the brain works much faster than speaking, use the time while another person is speaking to plan your next comment or question.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 34.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["Body language and voice convey the same message.","Use open-ended and closed questions at appropriate times.","Since the brain works much faster than speaking, use the time while another person is speaking to plan your next comment or question.","Use a paraphrasing technique to clarify your understanding of what was said."],"sourceQuestion":34,"stem":"All but one of the following represents good communicating skill. Which one does not?","sub":"cmq-management","why":"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>C. Since the brain works much faster than speaking, use the time while another person is speaking to plan your next comment or question.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 34.</span>"},"revision":"4d77b43b29b376425b16f5fbde6664331402596b47afabc882a28174ea470660"},"cmq:set-1:source-35":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"Arrange for an interpreter to be available when you meet with your business contact, unless you are fluent in the language and knowledgeable of the culture and business customs of the country.\",\"Plan an elaborate visual presentation that you will make shortly after arrival, and follow that by quickly striving to reach an agreement or make the sale.\",\"Resolve to keep your political views and personal beliefs to yourself even though you have strong feelings about the political climate and beliefs prevalent in the country you will visit.\",\"Obtain and study information about the country before leaving for your trip.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":35,\"stem\":\"As part of your preparation for a business trip to another country it would be wise to do all but one of the following. Which one would that be?\",\"sub\":\"cmq-management\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>B. Plan an elaborate visual presentation that you will make shortly after arrival, and follow that by quickly striving to reach an agreement or make the sale.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 35.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["Arrange for an interpreter to be available when you meet with your business contact, unless you are fluent in the language and knowledgeable of the culture and business customs of the country.","Plan an elaborate visual presentation that you will make shortly after arrival, and follow that by quickly striving to reach an agreement or make the sale.","Resolve to keep your political views and personal beliefs to yourself even though you have strong feelings about the political climate and beliefs prevalent in the country you will visit.","Obtain and study information about the country before leaving for your trip."],"sourceQuestion":35,"stem":"As part of your preparation for a business trip to another country it would be wise to do all but one of the following. Which one would that be?","sub":"cmq-management","why":"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>B. Plan an elaborate visual presentation that you will make shortly after arrival, and follow that by quickly striving to reach an agreement or make the sale.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 35.</span>"},"revision":"92e15d7a1b2b5d8bcf5420fc8f3a9542b3d128a96d23ddebf71cd9c12621f891"},"cmq:set-1:source-36":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"III only\",\"I, II, and IV\",\"I and IV only\",\"III and IV only\"],\"sourceQuestion\":36,\"stem\":\"Which of the following factors would be most critical to consider early when contemplating a conversion of a \\\"brick and mortar\\\" retail business to an e- business? I. What changes to the customer database are likely and what the ramifications of those changes are II. What image our new faceless organization will provide to the buying public III. Should IT be outsourced? IV. What internal impacts will the change from a personal service orientation to a transaction-processing orientation have on the workforce we employ and the technology approach we select?\",\"sub\":\"cmq-management\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>B. I, II, and IV</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 36.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["III only","I, II, and IV","I and IV only","III and IV only"],"sourceQuestion":36,"stem":"Which of the following factors would be most critical to consider early when contemplating a conversion of a \"brick and mortar\" retail business to an e- business? I. What changes to the customer database are likely and what the ramifications of those changes are II. What image our new faceless organization will provide to the buying public III. Should IT be outsourced? IV. What internal impacts will the change from a personal service orientation to a transaction-processing orientation have on the workforce we employ and the technology approach we select?","sub":"cmq-management","why":"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>B. I, II, and IV</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 36.</span>"},"revision":"944fa29f48d21b57945f2ad03a3dca21def8348e50e186b95da6c1cf2e0e04cf"},"cmq:set-1:source-37":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"Contract with a call center to handle customer complaints.\",\"Set up an informational Web site to display flowers available.\",\"Implement a GIS mapping system to more effectively allocate growing space based on growth requirements of the flowers, soil conditions, sunlight, and irrigation channels.\",\"Provide field workers with portable devices for recording flower growth, quality factors, and yield - for downloading nightly to a program to compute productivity, quality status, and potential yield by type of crop and when it will be available for shipment.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":37,\"stem\":\"To gain a competitive edge, a commercial flower grower seeks a technology solution that will improve productivity, quality, customer satisfaction, and profits. Which of the following actions would provide the best results within one year?\",\"sub\":\"cmq-management\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>D. Provide field workers with portable devices for recording flower growth, quality factors, and yield - for downloading nightly to a program to compute productivity, quality status, and potential yield by type of crop and when it will be available for shipment.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 37.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["Contract with a call center to handle customer complaints.","Set up an informational Web site to display flowers available.","Implement a GIS mapping system to more effectively allocate growing space based on growth requirements of the flowers, soil conditions, sunlight, and irrigation channels.","Provide field workers with portable devices for recording flower growth, quality factors, and yield - for downloading nightly to a program to compute productivity, quality status, and potential yield by type of crop and when it will be available for shipment."],"sourceQuestion":37,"stem":"To gain a competitive edge, a commercial flower grower seeks a technology solution that will improve productivity, quality, customer satisfaction, and profits. Which of the following actions would provide the best results within one year?","sub":"cmq-management","why":"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>D. Provide field workers with portable devices for recording flower growth, quality factors, and yield - for downloading nightly to a program to compute productivity, quality status, and potential yield by type of crop and when it will be available for shipment.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 37.</span>"},"revision":"32b9fb4169cdd451baec2b8ee47975bc9f32ef065306874ce2c0f263d77a8843"},"cmq:set-1:source-38":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"I, II, and III only\",\"I, II, III, and IV\",\"III and IV only\",\"I and II only\"