on":39,"stem":"An external risk factor that might need to be considered when conducting project planning is:","sub":"cmq-management","why":"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>B. Regulatory requirements.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 39.</span>"},"revision":"d1d7e3e4c45ef703f356778d6099f2e8c03061a71df2175fd166fc94cf3ffa39"},"cmq:set-1:source-4":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"Deliverables were completed on time, but project incurred a one percent cost overrun.\",\"Project team worked well together and worked hard but lacked sufficient resources to complete project on time and within budget.\",\"Project required a reduction in scope in order to finish within planned time and cost and avoid a late penalty.\",\"Project completed deliverables a week late and incurred a cost overrun but provided unplanned added value.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":4,\"stem\":\"Which of the following process improvement teams'' projects is likely to be regarded as most successful where on-time deliverables are critical.\",\"sub\":\"cmq-management\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>A. Deliverables were completed on time, but project incurred a one percent cost overrun.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 4.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["Deliverables were completed on time, but project incurred a one percent cost overrun.","Project team worked well together and worked hard but lacked sufficient resources to complete project on time and within budget.","Project required a reduction in scope in order to finish within planned time and cost and avoid a late penalty.","Project completed deliverables a week late and incurred a cost overrun but provided unplanned added value."],"sourceQuestion":4,"stem":"Which of the following process improvement teams'' projects is likely to be regarded as most successful where on-time deliverables are critical.","sub":"cmq-management","why":"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>A. Deliverables were completed on time, but project incurred a one percent cost overrun.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 4.</span>"},"revision":"c97f883d3816d9fa2ce49f50d2dc7d74eb1835f867e458c7b4c346a65f2d27cc"},"cmq:set-1:source-40":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"It is easier to accurately estimate benefits than costs.\",\"It is easier to accurately estimate costs than benefits.\",\"It is an elaborate tool requiring extensive computer support.\",\"It is too difficult to compute the time value of money.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":40,\"stem\":\"Which of the following is the biggest problem in cost-benefit analysis?\",\"sub\":\"cmq-management\",\"why\":\"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>B. It is easier to accurately estimate costs than benefits.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 40.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["It is easier to accurately estimate benefits than costs.","It is easier to accurately estimate costs than benefits.","It is an elaborate tool requiring extensive computer support.","It is too difficult to compute the time value of money."],"sourceQuestion":40,"stem":"Which of the following is the biggest problem in cost-benefit analysis?","sub":"cmq-management","why":"This response best applies the relevant management, communication, project, financial, or risk-management principle. <b>B. It is easier to accurately estimate costs than benefits.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 40.</span>"},"revision":"2ad95491730b4a56