ded as part of the total product package III. Monitoring of broad market trends IV. Observing customers using the product or service","sub":"cmq-customer","why":"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>D. III and IV only</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 88.</span>"},"revision":"1918071b20dc292f6b9bd8cd712479d34eadfea5c8feae10a827c1a308455c86"},"cmq:set-1:source-89":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"I, VI, IV, II, V, III\",\"I, II, V, VI, III, IV\",\"IV, I, II, VI, V, III\",\"VI, I, II, V, IV, III\"],\"sourceQuestion\":89,\"stem\":\"Which sequence is most appropriate for administering a customer satisfaction survey, from beginning to end? I. Prepare the survey instrument; II. Administer the survey; III. Report the results; IV. Identify survey objectives; V. Analyze the data; VI. Organize the data.\",\"sub\":\"cmq-customer\",\"why\":\"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>C. IV, I, II, VI, V, III</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 89.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["I, VI, IV, II, V, III","I, II, V, VI, III, IV","IV, I, II, VI, V, III","VI, I, II, V, IV, III"],"sourceQuestion":89,"stem":"Which sequence is most appropriate for administering a customer satisfaction survey, from beginning to end? I. Prepare the survey instrument; II. Administer the survey; III. Report the results; IV. Identify survey objectives; V. Analyze the data; VI. Organize the data.","sub":"cmq-customer","why":"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>C. IV, I, II, VI, V, III</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 89.</span>"},"revision":"b2b42301af1c79eea30201c01a8317c4d7f633dbc1f6ad847f64a88d393453db"},"cmq:set-1:source-9":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"A SWOT analysis\",\"Hoshin planning and deployment\",\"A seven-step problem-solving technique\",\"Scenario planning\"],\"sourceQuestion\":9,\"stem\":\"Strategic planning may include all but which of the following?\",\"sub\":\"cmq-strategy\",\"why\":\"This response best aligns the decision with sound strategic planning, environmental analysis, deployment, and measurement. <b>C. A seven-step problem-solving technique</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 9.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["A SWOT analysis","Hoshin planning and deployment","A seven-step problem-solving technique","Scenario planning"],"sourceQuestion":9,"stem":"Strategic planning may include all but which of the following?","sub":"cmq-strategy","why":"This response best aligns the decision with sound strategic planning, environmental analysis, deployment, and measurement. <b>C. A seven-step problem-solving technique</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 9.</span>"},"revision":"32e2e5364cf43cb0fa0a6228a371e7484b4cf199a77fbb773e5af2e8d7a47695"},"cmq:set-1:source-90":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"Focus groups\",\"Market test\",\"Trade-off analysis\",\"In-person interview\"],\"sourceQuestion\":90,\"stem\":\"Which of the following is the most direct technique for measuring customer value?\",\"sub\":\"cmq-customer\",\"why\":\"Trade-off analysis directly measures the value customers assign to competing product or service attributes by requiring explicit preference choices. Interviews collect qualitative input but do not inherently quantify value trade-offs. <b>C. Trade-off analysis</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 90; answer corrected for student use.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["Focus groups","Market test","Trade-off analysis","In-person interview"],"sourceQuestion":90,"stem":"Which of the following is the most direct technique for measuring customer value?","sub":"cmq-customer","why":"Trade-off analysis directly measures the value customers assign to competing product or service attributes by requiring explicit preference choices. Interviews collect qualitative input but do not inherently quantify value trade-offs. <b>C. Trade-off analysis</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 90; answer corrected for student use.</span>"},"revision":"2054fe9de0fc420c6861c99ca4105781db54646b105be0ca34b4c09e28e0e50a"},"cmq:set-1:source-91":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"Customer wants/needs\",\"Company product/process characteristics\",\"Competitor product performance\",\"Customer service training requirements\"],\"sourceQuestion\":91,\"stem\":\"Quality function deployment looks at the relationship between all but which of the following components?\",\"sub\":\"cmq-customer\",\"why\":\"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>D. Customer service training requirements</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 91.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["Customer wants/needs","Company product/process characteristics","Competitor product performance","Customer service training requirements"],"sourceQuestion":91,"stem":"Quality function deployment looks at the relationship between all but which of the following components?","sub":"cmq-customer","why":"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>D. Customer service training requirements</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 91.</span>"},"revision":"bc6f25ba08dbfb377b1c4eee1059002a1af1ffe5e1c679879ae983822d270c6b"},"cmq:set-1:source-92":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"I, II, III, and IV\",\"IV only\",\"I, II, and IV only\",\"II and III only\"],\"sourceQuestion\":92,\"stem\":\"A focus group consisting of external customers would be useful to: I. Collect data that can be used to construct a customer survey. II. Test the acceptability of a proposed new service. III. Validate customer satisfaction across the entire customer base. IV. Identify ways an existing service could be improved.\",\"sub\":\"cmq-customer\",\"why\":\"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>C. I, II, and IV only</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 92.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["I, II, III, and IV","IV only","I, II, and IV only","II and III only"],"sourceQuestion":92,"stem":"A focus group consisting of external customers would be useful to: I. Collect data that can be used to construct a customer survey. II. Test the acceptability of a proposed new service. III. Validate customer satisfaction across the entire customer base. IV. Identify ways an existing service could be improved.","sub":"cmq-customer","why":"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>C. I, II, and IV only</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 92.</span>"},"revision":"5d77a23507b6eb6d69d342df28a6888046d451f6a02a5b25dfdadf38f6e238c3"},"cmq:set-1:source-93":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"Use of random sampling to collect audit information.\",\"Management by walking around (MBWA) for the retail industry.\",\"Anonymous observation of customer service practices.\",\"Verification of accuracy and reliability of sales data.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":93,\"stem\":\"Mystery shopping is a term that applies to:\",\"sub\":\"cmq-customer\",\"why\":\"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>C. Anonymous observation of customer service practices.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 93.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["Use of random sampling to collect audit information.","Management by walking around (MBWA) for the retail industry.","Anonymous observation of customer service practices.","Verification of accuracy and reliability of sales data."],"sourceQuestion":93,"stem":"Mystery shopping is a term that applies to:","sub":"cmq-customer","why":"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>C. Anonymous observation of customer service practices.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 93.</span>"},"revision":"9b8068a37e918c536fad272735852450378723510ee631a9da75c442fef5a742"},"cmq:set-1:source-94":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"Hire and train qualified staff and reward them based on performance.\",\"Get to know the customers'' most pressing needs.\",\"Develop a strategic alliance/partnership with key customers.\",\"Get management commitment to a focus on customers.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":94,\"stem\":\"The first step in a successful customer satisfaction program is to:\",\"sub\":\"cmq-customer\",\"why\":\"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>D. Get management commitment to a focus on customers.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 94.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["Hire and train qualified staff and reward them based on performance.","Get to know the customers'' most pressing needs.","Develop a strategic alliance/partnership with key customers.","Get management commitment to a focus on customers."],"sourceQuestion":94,"stem":"The first step in a successful customer satisfaction program is to:","sub":"cmq-customer","why":"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>D. Get management commitment to a focus on customers.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 94.</span>"},"revision":"157ac8b27dc331a0e3089d5e2809fcb433c37d776d0b9408fda3e3ffd99bcd79"},"cmq:set-1:source-95":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"Physical place in the facility where employees gather to discuss comments heard from customers.\",\"Place where customer comments, pro and con, are posted for all employees to see.\",\"Practice whereby surveillance personnel periodically listen in to ongoing conversations between employees and customers for the purpose of identifying employee behavior that can be improved.\",\"Designated individual or group trained to listen carefully to customer comments, and record the comments in a process where the comments can be analyzed (trended) and actions taken to improve customer satisfaction.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":95,\"stem\":\"A listening post is a:\",\"sub\":\"cmq-customer\",\"why\":\"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>D. Designated individual or group trained to listen carefully to customer comments, and record the comments in a process where the comments can be analyzed (trended) and actions taken to improve customer satisfaction.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 95.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["Physical place in the facility where employees gather to discuss comments heard from customers.","Place where customer comments, pro and con, are posted for all employees to see.","Practice whereby surveillance personnel periodically listen in to ongoing conversations between employees and customers for the purpose of identifying employee behavior that can be improved.","Designated individual or group trained to listen carefully to customer comments, and record the comments in a process where the comments can be analyzed (trended) and actions taken to improve customer satisfaction."],"sourceQuestion":95,"stem":"A listening post is a:","sub":"cmq-customer","why":"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>D. Designated individual or group trained to listen carefully to customer comments, and record the comments in a process where the comments can be analyzed (trended) and actions taken to improve customer satisfaction.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 95.</span>"},"revision":"277c543264648fdf77c607fa6058f34a3f6211571bc970d39678e39342f3799d"},"cmq:set-1:source-96":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"I only\",\"I, II, III, and IV\",\"I and II only\",\"I, II, and IV only\"],\"sourceQuestion\":96,\"stem\":\"In the development of a consumer appliance product survey which of the following data would likely aid the process? I. An analysis of customer complaints received II. Satisfaction data from a customer focus group III. Number of product defects detected prior to shipments IV. Warranty registration data\",\"sub\":\"cmq-customer\",\"why\":\"Complaints, focus-group satisfaction data, and warranty registrations all contain customer-facing evidence useful in designing a consumer survey. Pre-shipment defect counts are internal process data rather than direct consumer input. <b>D. I, II, and IV only</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 96; answer corrected for student use.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["I only","I, II, III, and IV","I and II only","I, II, and IV only"],"sourceQuestion":96,"stem":"In the development of a consumer appliance product survey which of the following data would likely aid the process? I. An analysis of customer complaints received II. Satisfaction data from a customer focus group III. Number of product defects detected prior to shipments IV. Warranty registration data","sub":"cmq-customer","why":"Complaints, focus-group satisfaction data, and warranty registrations all contain customer-facing evidence useful in designing a consumer survey. Pre-shipment defect counts are internal process data rather than direct consumer input. <b>D. I, II, and IV only</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 96; answer corrected for student use.</span>"},"revision":"cbedebc380ae59e1cebc877417510ae801342dc02325b36753d7414ab3503134"},"cmq:set-1:source-97":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"I and III only\",\"I, II, III, and IV\",\"II, III, and IV only\",\"I only\"],\"sourceQuestion\":97,\"stem\":\"To further improve customer loyalty, an investment service organization may effectively use which of the following strategies? I. A lost-customer analysis II. Free lessons for customers on how to make wise investments III. A customer panel to determine acceptability of a free quarterly newsletter highlighting the lives of long-term investors IV. Direct computer access to market information and investment analysis data for high-value customers\",\"sub\":\"cmq-customer\",\"why\":\"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>B. I, II, III, and IV</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 97.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["I and III only","I, II, III, and IV","II, III, and IV only","I only"],"sourceQuestion":97,"stem":"To further improve customer loyalty, an investment service organization may effectively use which of the following strategies? I. A lost-customer analysis II. Free lessons for customers on how to make wise investments III. A customer panel to determine acceptability of a free quarterly newsletter highlighting the lives of long-term investors IV. Direct computer access to market information and investment analysis data for high-value customers","sub":"cmq-customer","why":"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>B. I, II, III, and IV</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 97.</span>"},"revision":"96ed178b0e2ab3564239e9da5eef7aa0d8d8601b5c208553a0fe4b0eadd87c17"},"cmq:set-1:source-98":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"Compare this cost from one accounting period to another.\",\"Compare lost-customer costs with costs to obtain new customers, and if the cost of obtaining new customers is greater, refocus efforts on customer retention.\",\"Use these figures to reprimand employees responsible for lost customers.\",\"Justify an initiative to contact lost customers and entice them to come back.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":98,\"stem\":\"The best use of the cost of lost banking customers is to:\",\"sub\":\"cmq-customer\",\"why\":\"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>B. Compare lost-customer costs with costs to obtain new customers, and if the cost of obtaining new customers is greater, refocus efforts on customer retention.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 98.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["Compare this cost from one accounting period to another.","Compare lost-customer costs with costs to obtain new customers, and if the cost of obtaining new customers is greater, refocus efforts on customer retention.","Use these figures to reprimand employees responsible for lost customers.","Justify an initiative to contact lost customers and entice them to come back."],"sourceQuestion":98,"stem":"The best use of the cost of lost banking customers is to:","sub":"cmq-customer","why":"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>B. Compare lost-customer costs with costs to obtain new customers, and if the cost of obtaining new customers is greater, refocus efforts on customer retention.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 98.</span>"},"revision":"c407770e2519e64c5069aab53ad04eb9ea827bbf94b2bb6b3ad4383e7bb4b11c"},"cmq:set-1:source-99":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"\\\"The customer is always right.\\\"\",\"When dealing with a problem, thank the customer for bringing the problem to you and allowing you to help resolve the problem.\",\"State your organization''s policy regarding handling of such problems.\",\"Be sure the customer realizes you are not responsible for the problem.\"],\"sourceQuestion\":99,\"stem\":\"One of the most important customer service principles to apply is:\",\"sub\":\"cmq-customer\",\"why\":\"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>B. When dealing with a problem, thank the customer for bringing the problem to you and allowing you to help resolve the problem.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: Pocket Study Guide CMQ-OE, Question 99.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["\"The customer is always right.\"","When dealing with a problem, thank the customer for bringing the problem to you and allowing you to help resolve the problem.","State your organization''s policy regarding handling of such problems.","Be sure the customer realizes you are not responsible for the problem."],"sourceQuestion":99,"stem":"One of the most important customer service principles to apply is:","sub":"cmq-customer","why":"This response best applies customer identification, segmentation, listening, relationship, or satisfaction principles. <b>B. When dealing with a problem, thank the customer for bringing the problem to you and allowing you to help resolve the problem.</b> <span class=\"tb-sourc