:3,"options":["0.2608","0.7392","0.86","0.9808"],"stem":"Two independent active-parallel components have reliabilities 0.88 and 0.84; either component can provide the required function. What is system reliability?","sub":"design","why":"Parallel reliability is one minus the probability that every path fails. R = 1 − (1−0.88)(1−0.84) = 0.9808."},"revision":"df9f4fc30998954e7de5a842f67079d4e24bf41e61adc356d847eac60c15eff8"},"cqe:set-2:legacy-41":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"96.49%\",\"3.51%\",\"96.36%\",\"27.5%\"],\"stem\":\"A repairable system has MTBF=275 hours and MTTR=10 hours. What is inherent availability?\",\"sub\":\"design\",\"why\":\"Availability = MTBF ÷ (MTBF + MTTR). A = 275/(275+10) = 96.49%.\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["96.49%","3.51%","96.36%","27.5%"],"stem":"A repairable system has MTBF=275 hours and MTTR=10 hours. What is inherent availability?","sub":"design","why":"Availability = MTBF ÷ (MTBF + MTTR). A = 275/(275+10) = 96.49%."},"revision":"1cd17060da14366d9bb3554ec5e545e26a6923c1ca0ed7c660384314c63a46d2"},"cqe:set-2:legacy-42":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"84\",\"5\",\"12\",\"15\"],\"stem\":\"An FMEA assigns severity=6, occurrence=2, and detection=7. What is the traditional RPN?\",\"sub\":\"design\",\"why\":\"Traditional RPN is severity × occurrence × detection. RPN = 6 × 2 × 7 = 84.\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["84","5","12","15"],"stem":"An FMEA assigns severity=6, occurrence=2, and detection=7. What is the traditional RPN?","sub":"design","why":"Traditional RPN is severity × occurrence × detection. RPN = 6 × 2 × 7 = 84."},"revision":"3b688de2956a6c47b13b2289f6719a055826cec77e111d94e73259f33a38ff57"},"cqe:set-2:legacy-43":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"A planned cross-functional review with qualified participants, including individuals not directly responsible for the design element being reviewed.\",\"The review occurs only after product launch\",\"The designer review