r success. Communicating the need for change is the first step in the change management process. [I.B.2]"},"revision":"c9ea61ff737833832160378d7546b252233962d1a0ecdc9dc49d89829dc3c9b3"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-184":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"SWOT analysis\",\"Readiness assessment\",\"Interrelationship digraph\",\"Stakeholder analysis\"],\"stem\":\"Which tool would be the best to use to assess an organization''s willingness to change its culture?\",\"sub\":\"p1\",\"why\":\"A readiness assessment can be used to determine an organization''s willingness to change. [I.B.3]\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["SWOT analysis","Readiness assessment","Interrelationship digraph","Stakeholder analysis"],"stem":"Which tool would be the best to use to assess an organization''s willingness to change its culture?","sub":"p1","why":"A readiness assessment can be used to determine an organization''s willingness to change. [I.B.3]"},"revision":"1b88fe8cdb21a158a5a65eaa83ec1c68e72c0369c50f15b3c10d60580c977a1d"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-185":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"causes and effects.\",\"strengths and weaknesses.\",\"driving and restraining forces.\",\"selection criteria.\"],\"stem\":\"When performing a force-field analysis, the team lists a desired state and then brainstorms:\",\"sub\":\"p1\",\"why\":\"A force-field analysis lists the project or goal and then brainstorms the forces that can drive or restrain success. [I.B.3]\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["causes and effects.","strengths and weaknesses.","driving and restraining forces.","selection criteria."],"stem":"When performing a force-field analysis, the team lists a desired state and then brainstorms:","sub":"p1","why":"A force-field analysis lists the project or goal and then brainstorms the forces that can drive or restrain success. [I.B.3]"},"revision":"2a56915fe080cdaab1f5e6d4c87d4606848032a1033476fdb70f56806c30e156"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-186":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"A view of the future state\",\"Goals and metrics\",\"New policies\",\"The need for change\"],\"stem\":\"Effective communication is essential to successfully implementing change. Which of the following items is typically communicated first?\",\"sub\":\"p1\",\"why\":\"Effective communication is considered essential for success. Communicating the need for change is the first step in the change management process. [I.B.3]\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["A view of the future state","Goals and metrics","New policies","The need for change"],"stem":"Effective communication is essential to successfully implementing change. Which of the following items is typically communicated first?","sub":"p1","why":"Effective communication is considered essential for success. Communicating the need for change is the first step in the change management process. [I.B.3]"},"revision":"d34b0fb1357b49ce0f786eed3ed69cb424c98e33c285b34cade113a84ae2b065"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-187":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"Matrix\",\"Cross-functional\",\"Centralized\",\"Decentralized\"],\"stem\":\"Which of the following types of organizational structure is most resistant to change?\",\"sub\":\"p1\",\"why\":\"A highly centralized organizational structure tends to resist any change, and fundamental improvements are difficult to achieve. [I.B.2]\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["Matrix","Cross-functional","Centralized","Decentralized"],"stem":"Which of the following types of organizational structure is most resistant to change?","sub":"p1","why":"A highly centralized organizational structure tends to resist any change, and fundamental improvements are difficult to achieve. [I.B.2]"},"revision":"c998dbd7dd1110a6c54356ca0d0d6688a796d9b1bd45843287ce2c52fa07fef6"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-188":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"SIPOC\",\"PDCA\",\"DMAIC\",\"DFSS\"],\"stem\":\"Which of the following models is the best for identifying stakeholders of a proposed change in a manufacturing process?\",\"sub\":\"p1\",\"why\":\"A SIPOC view identifies suppliers, inputs, the process, outputs, and customers, helping the team identify stakeholders affected by a proposed change. [I.B.3]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["SIPOC","PDCA","DMAIC","DFSS"],"stem":"Which of the following models is the best for identifying stakeholders of a proposed change in a manufacturing process?","sub":"p1","why":"A SIPOC view identifies suppliers, inputs, the process, outputs, and customers, helping the team identify stakeholders affected by a proposed change. [I.B.3]"},"revision":"a16d02bdafbf2fd02668279836042d699546f86788dfd04b09c42c0f0f66e6ff"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-189":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"provide frequent communications.\",\"appoint a management representative.\",\"delegate the responsibilities to a qualified consultant.\",\"divide the responsibility and authority equally between management and the workers.\"],\"stem\":\"To maintain support throughout the change life cycle, the organization must:\",\"sub\":\"p1\",\"why\":\"Frequent communication of project status throughout the change cycle is essential to maintaining stakeholder support. [I.B.3]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["provide frequent communications.","appoint a management representative.","delegate the responsibilities to a qualified consultant.","divide the responsibility and authority equally between management and the workers."],"stem":"To maintain support throughout the change life cycle, the organization must:","sub":"p1","why":"Frequent communication of project status throughout the change cycle is essential to maintaining stakeholder support. [I.B.3]"},"revision":"de855b421b72d91fa3d030cc689256fe4b5995b351b05d0cd1f0d9f0399f7328"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-19":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"nonsupportive.\",\"supportive.\",\"a mixed blessing.\",\"marginal.\"],\"stem\":\"A stakeholder who has been designated as low potential for cooperation and high potential to impact a project would be considered:\",\"sub\":\"p2\",\"why\":\"A stakeholder with low potential for cooperation and high potential to affect the project is classified as nonsupportive. [II.A]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["nonsupportive.","supportive.","a mixed blessing.","marginal."],"stem":"A stakeholder who has been designated as low potential for cooperation and high potential to impact a project would be considered:","sub":"p2","why":"A stakeholder with low potential for cooperation and high potential to affect the project is classified as nonsupportive. [II.A]"},"revision":"eee6c41b88199fff12dac79c77967038b0c715f47bea32856b26816c486fbcc6"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-190":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"Presentation, data collection, statistical analysis, and planning\",\"Presentation, analysis, and implementation\",\"Planning, data collection, analysis, and implementation\",\"Planning, detection factors, statistical analysis, and integration\"],\"stem\":\"The benchmarking process usually follows which sequence?\",\"sub\":\"p2\",\"why\":\"The benchmarking process follows the cycle of planning, data collection, analysis, and implementation. [II.B]\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["Presentation, data collection, statistical analysis, and planning","Presentation, analysis, and implementation","Planning, data collection, analysis, and implementation","Planning, detection factors, statistical analysis, and integration"],"stem":"The benchmarking process usually follows which sequence?","sub":"p2","why":"The benchmarking process follows the cycle of planning, data collection, analysis, and implementation. [II.B]"},"revision":"0d9ecf000b4b1547e5aececad50ff0f53a201417f687ea990f6ef07cf4ce8c50"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-191":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"Breaches of confidentiality\",\"Longer process cycle time\",\"Higher process capability\",\"Improved customer satisfaction\"],\"stem\":\"Which benchmarking risk should be controlled through confidentiality agreements and a code of conduct?\",\"sub\":\"p2\",\"why\":\"Benchmarking may expose confidential or proprietary information. Confidentiality agreements and a code of conduct help control that risk. [II.B]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["Breaches of confidentiality","Longer process cycle time","Higher process capability","Improved customer satisfaction"],"stem":"Which benchmarking risk should be controlled through confidentiality agreements and a code of conduct?","sub":"p2","why":"Benchmarking may expose confidential or proprietary information. Confidentiality agreements and a code of conduct help control that risk. [II.B]"},"revision":"3c58ddb2728f245589bf5b4301663d07d53f91d0b345155808182849d49ad5d3"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-192":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"Financial perspective\",\"Learning and growth perspective\",\"Internal business processes perspective\",\"Customer perspective\"],\"stem\":\"In a balanced scorecard, which perspective addresses shareholder value?\",\"sub\":\"p2\",\"why\":\"The financial perspective provides insight into how well goals, objectives, and strategies are contributing to shareholder value and the bottom line. [II.C.1]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["Financial perspective","Learning and growth perspective","Internal business processes perspective","Customer perspective"],"stem":"In a balanced scorecard, which perspective addresses shareholder value?","sub":"p2","why":"The financial perspective provides insight into how well goals, objectives, and strategies are contributing to shareholder value and the bottom line. [II.C.1]"},"revision":"e6785164e860a9ff1b15b60dd6e42e45fce625ee2db006811bd941ff617dfa75"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-193":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"Customer referrals\",\"Customer complaints\",\"Customer abandonment rate\",\"Competitive market share\"],\"stem\":\"An organization''s net promoter score is positively correlated