 4\",\"Area 9\"],\"stem\":\"Using the numbered house-of-quality diagram below, in which area are customer requirements listed?\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"Customer requirements are listed along the left side of the house of quality, in Area 1. [IV.A.3]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"chart":{"type":"house-of-quality"},"options":["Area 1","Area 2","Area 4","Area 9"],"stem":"Using the numbered house-of-quality diagram below, in which area are customer requirements listed?","sub":"def","why":"Customer requirements are listed along the left side of the house of quality, in Area 1. [IV.A.3]"},"revision":"7c9fb7d06e71eb952753697a3bd667ded7b7deaa0b55d89b4ded68092998c45f"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-256":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"appease the finance department.\",\"set the team up for failure.\",\"avoid suboptimizing the process.\",\"satisfy the project champion.\"],\"stem\":\"A Six Sigma project is chartered to increase on-time deliveries. The team has decided that it will track two metrics: on-time deliveries as well as shipping cost. Shipping cost has likely been added to the project metrics to:\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"The team must track both on-time deliveries and shipping costs so that the overall delivery process is not suboptimized. [IV.B.5]\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["appease the finance department.","set the team up for failure.","avoid suboptimizing the process.","satisfy the project champion."],"stem":"A Six Sigma project is chartered to increase on-time deliveries. The team has decided that it will track two metrics: on-time deliveries as well as shipping cost. Shipping cost has likely been added to the project metrics to:","sub":"def","why":"The team must track both on-time deliveries and shipping costs so that the overall delivery process is not suboptimized. [IV.B.5]"},"revision":"1203b1bc76ff5f248721a934ca15a06f41e9d5dbfa8f3f5a1677a83feb6c96ab"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-257":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"an increase in quality and a decrease in cost.\",\"a decrease in duration and quality.\",\"an increase in duration and cost.\",\"a decrease in cost and quality.\"],\"stem\":\"An increase in project scope can result in:\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"Increasing project scope can lead to an increase in the project''s duration as well as increased costs. [IV.B.3]\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["an increase in quality and a decrease in cost.","a decrease in duration and quality.","an increase in duration and cost.","a decrease in cost and quality."],"stem":"An increase in project scope can result in:","sub":"def","why":"Increasing project scope can lead to an increase in the project''s duration as well as increased costs. [IV.B.3]"},"revision":"7501daa4856b54472eb5a51ddaf868bdf865f64d30e7a718778de488be6f5700"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-258":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"Gantt chart.\",\"affinity diagram.\",\"tree diagram.\",\"interrelationship diagram.\"],\"stem\":\"The project management tool that allows the team to see planned and completed tasks on a timeline is the:\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"A Gantt chart shows planned and completed tasks on a timeline. [IV.C.1]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["Gantt chart.","affinity diagram.","tree diagram.","interrelationship diagram."],"stem":"The project management tool that allows the team to see planned and completed tasks on a timeline is the:","sub":"def","why":"A Gantt chart shows planned and completed tasks on a timeline. [IV.C.1]"},"revision":"66829846b213428812a8ea5bc50862b2418c08173eb6a263892c7e05416957ff"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-259":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"dependencies.\",\"critical tasks.\",\"primary tasks.\",\"secondary tasks.\"],\"stem\":\"In a Gantt chart, task C cannot be started until tasks A and B are completed. Tasks A and B would be considered:\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"If task C cannot begin before tasks A and B are completed, then A and B are considered dependencies, or predecessor tasks. [IV.C.1]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["dependencies.","critical tasks.","primary tasks.","secondary tasks."],"stem":"In a Gantt chart, task C cannot be started until tasks A and B are completed. Tasks A and B would be considered:","sub":"def","why":"If task C cannot begin before tasks A and B are completed, then A and B are considered dependencies, or predecessor tasks. [IV.C.1]"},"revision":"03ef30af7323c74ccb5c3ac2a882648e6a26eb7a58859fa198d9185602cf7ad4"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-26":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"has not been fully defined.\",\"is fully mapped.\",\"is not industry specific.\",\"was provided by a consultant.\"],\"stem\":\"The benchmarking process can be ineffective if it:\",\"sub\":\"p2\",\"why\":\"Benchmarking requires a defined, planned, and funded methodology. A poorly defined benchmarking effort is likely to fail. [II.B]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["has not been fully defined.","is fully mapped.","is not industry specific.","was provided by a consultant."],"stem":"The benchmarking process can be ineffective if it:","sub":"p2","why":"Benchmarking requires a defined, planned, and funded methodology. A poorly defined benchmarking effort is likely to fail. [II.B]"},"revision":"a8e527733fe730ee19c60c72758134bbf8fbe1acd52f4c5a276ccce7486e86dd"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-260":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"tollgate reviews\",\"Gantt charts\",\"interrelationship diagrams\",\"work breakdown structures\"],\"stem\":\"What is used to verify that all required activities for one DMAIC phase are complete before the team moves to the next phase?\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"Tollgate reviews are formal meetings held with the project sponsor after each of the DMAIC steps. During the meeting, the sponsor ensures that all the activities for a phase are completed before the team moves on to the next phase. [IV.C.2]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["tollgate reviews","Gantt charts","interrelationship diagrams","work breakdown structures"],"stem":"What is used to verify that all required activities for one DMAIC phase are complete before the team moves to the next phase?","sub":"def","why":"Tollgate reviews are formal meetings held with the project sponsor after each of the DMAIC steps. During the meeting, the sponsor ensures that all the activities for a phase are completed before the team moves on to the next phase. [IV.C.2]"},"revision":"a812e58256bbb84b1475b52d2f4d00a89cb4a123d2f2dfdd82d40960f2210fe9"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-261":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"Will we run a pilot?\",\"What are the critical Xs?\",\"Who are the stakeholders?\",\"What did the FMEA show?\"],\"stem\":\"A typical question a champion may ask in a tollgate review for the Analyze phase may be:\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"The purpose of the Analyze tollgate, among other things, is to present the critical Xs of the process and establish root causes. [IV.C.2]\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["Will we run a pilot?","What are the critical Xs?","Who are the stakeholders?","What did the FMEA show?"],"stem":"A typical question a champion may ask in a tollgate review for the Analyze phase may be:","sub":"def","why":"The purpose of the Analyze tollgate, among other things, is to present the critical Xs of the process and establish root causes. [IV.C.2]"},"revision":"e99b199a854ba6899ae89699d7ac0276c0b7624e1aa089f428787a321d4ab43e"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-262":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"To locate which machines need repair\",\"To document where the team is failing\",\"To subdivide larger tasks into smaller tasks\",\"To find the critical path of the project plan\"],\"stem\":\"What is the purpose of a work breakdown structure?\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"In a work breakdown structure, large tasks are systematically broken down into smaller and smaller tasks. These small tasks can then be assigned to individuals. [IV.C.3]\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["To locate which machines need repair","To document where the team is failing","To subdivide larger tasks into smaller tasks","To find the critical path of the project plan"],"stem":"What is the purpose of a work breakdown structure?","sub":"def","why":"In a work breakdown structure, large tasks are systematically broken down into smaller and smaller tasks. These small tasks can then be assigned to individuals. [IV.C.3]"},"revision":"01ec578236efc758d9205c785f55fabe60afd375c8932e7cff4fe1e336122f36"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-263":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"tree diagram.\",\"interrelationship diagram.\",\"Gantt chart.\",\"work breakdown structure.\"],\"stem\":\"A tool used to show the activities, subactivities, costs, time, and materials necessary to complete a goal is the:\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"A work breakdown structure starts with the larger goal and then systematically breaks each activity into smaller and smaller subactivities or tasks. At the final stage, costs, time, and material information are also collected. [IV.C.3]\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["tree diagram.","interrelationship diagram.","Gantt chart.","work breakdown structure."],"stem":"A tool used to show the activities, subactivities, costs, time, and materials necessary to complete a goal is the:","sub":"def","why":"A work breakdown structure starts with the larger goal and then systematically breaks each activity into smaller and smaller subactivities or tasks. At the final stage, costs, time, and material information are also collected. [IV.C.3]"},"revision":"6f387a335e4fe7f1b3fbfe43404a96bd9ccb8c011aa14615415d34499a77e0e2"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-264":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"Responsible\",\"Accountable\",\"Consulted\",\"Informed\"],\"stem\":\"In which role in a RACI model must a decision be discussed with the individual before a final decision is made?\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"The RACI model is a matrix that lists stakeholders and tasks, and then indicates who is responsible, accountable, consulted, and informed for each task. A stakeholder in the \\\"consulted\\\" role must be asked about a decision before a final decision is made. [IV.C.4]\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["Responsible","Accountable","Consulted","Informed"],"stem":"In which role in a RACI model must a decision be discussed with the individual before a final decision is made?","sub":"def","why":"The RACI model is a matrix that lists stakeholders and tasks, and then indicates who is responsible, accountable, consulted, and informed for each task. A stakeholder in the \"consulted\" role must be asked about a decision before a final decision is made. [IV.C.4]"},"revision":"8dce68459f12dfef2fdb8798c3c519087019d0239672ae3fc0c4d8872134d085"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-265":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"Responsible\",\"Accountable\",\"Consulted\",\"Informed\"],\"stem\":\"In which role in the RACI model must the individual be cognizant about a decision because they are affected?\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"The RACI model is a matrix that lists stakeholders and tasks, and then indicates who is responsible, accountable, consulted, and informed for each task. A stakeholder in the \\\"informed\\\" role must be informed about a decision because they are affected. [IV.C.4]\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["Responsible","Accountable","Consulted","Informed"],"stem":"In which role in the RACI model must the individual be cognizant about a decision because they are affected?","sub":"def","why":"The RACI model is a matrix that lists stakeholders and tasks, and then indicates who is responsible, accountable, consulted, and informed for each task. A stakeholder in the \"informed\" role must be informed about a decision because they are affected. [IV.C.4]"},"revision":"2e07ca3745fe6a696254779ed43dd622d420a8ef8ce7f0a8c92592cc0a4825c7"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-266":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"are suggested from the ideas themselves.\",\"are predetermined.\",\"are generated in a separate brainstorming session on the categories.\",\"are determined by the organizer.\"],\"stem\":\"In an affinity diagram, the themes into which the ideas are grouped:\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"The themes into which ideas are grouped in an affinity diagram are suggested by the ideas themselves. [IV.D.1]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["are suggested from the ideas themselves.","are predetermined.","are generated in a separate brainstorming session on the categories.","are determined by the organizer."],"stem":"In an affinity diagram, the themes into which the ideas are grouped:","sub":"def","why":"The themes into which ideas are grouped in an affinity diagram are suggested by the ideas themselves. [IV.D.1]"},"revision":"acb66dafd81750ece1aa40488464d8de83ddd010b3bb0f30f0fd34f78aea6675"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-267":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"Activity network diagram\",\"Process decision program chart\",\"Affinity diagram\",\"Interrelationship digraph\"],\"stem\":\"Which tool should be used when the issue at hand is ill-defined or difficult to grasp, and group consensus is needed?\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"If an issue is ill-defined or difficult to grasp, the best tool to use is an affinity diagram, in which brainstormed ideas are arranged into natural groups through a group consensus. [IV.D.1]\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["Activity network diagram","Process decision program chart","Affinity diagram","Interrelationship digraph"],"stem":"Which tool should be used when the issue at hand is ill-defined or difficult to grasp, and group consensus is needed?","sub":"def","why":"If an issue is ill-defined or difficult to grasp, the best tool to use is an affinity diagram, in which brainstormed ideas are arranged into natural groups through a group consensus. [IV.D.1]"},"revision":"b1db57fb7f0f4c7bc05d7ea6f27a3452ab3fd9e420cf167a86aae39f60efb83a"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-268":{"can