team will pass through which two final stages?\",\"sub\":\"tm\",\"why\":\"After the first four team phases, adjourning was added as a final stage to acknowledge the team''s life cycle and distinct end point. Recognition was then added to ensure that the team is properly recognized for its accomplishments. [III.B.2]\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["Forming and norming","Rewarding and recognition","Performing and adjourning","Adjourning and recognition"],"stem":"After the first four team growth stages, a team will pass through which two final stages?","sub":"tm","why":"After the first four team phases, adjourning was added as a final stage to acknowledge the team''s life cycle and distinct end point. Recognition was then added to ensure that the team is properly recognized for its accomplishments. [III.B.2]"},"revision":"b5eca00cfbcda3a0114e7bdf3f5b2c3d734ce014990806686f81f073a8db0a53"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-410":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"chart\":{\"columns\":[\"Degrees of freedom\",\"One-tailed α = 0.05 critical t\"],\"rows\":[[\"20\",\"1.725\"],[\"21\",\"1.721\"],[\"22\",\"1.717\"],[\"23\",\"1.714\"]],\"type\":\"data-table\"},\"options\":[\"−1.868\",\"−1.717\",\"−1.714\",\"−1.645\"],\"stem\":\"A Black Belt calculates a sample correlation of −0.37 using n = 24 pairs of observations. Using the Student''s t reference excerpt below, what is the critical value for the lower-tail test H₀: ρ = 0 versus H₁: ρ is less than 0 at α = 0.05?\",\"sub\":\"ana\",\"why\":\"The correlation test uses a Student''s t distribution with n − 2 = 22 degrees of freedom. The table gives t = 1.717 for a one-tailed α = 0.05 test. Because this is a lower-tail test, the critical value is −1.717. [VI.A.1]\"}","content":{"answer":1,"chart":{"columns":["Degrees of freedom","One-tailed α = 0.05 critical t"],"rows":[["20","1.725"],["21","1.721"],["22","1.717"],["23","1.714"]],"type":"data-table"},"options":["−1.868","−1.717","−1.714","−1.645"],"stem":"A Black Belt calculates a sample correlation of −0.37 using n = 24 pairs of observations. Using the Student''s t reference excerpt below, what is the critical value for the lower-tail test H₀: ρ = 0 versus H₁: ρ is less than 0 at α = 0.05?","sub":"ana","why":"The correlation test uses a Student''s t distribution with n − 2 = 22 degrees of freedom. The table gives t = 1.717 for a one-tailed α = 0.05 test. Because this is a lower-tail test, the critical value is −1.717. [VI.A.1]"},"revision":"830e771403b8347b30e4409865d704440e0bf1d29e6e633577664c7243aa9649"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-411":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"chart\":{\"columns\":[\"Observation\",\"X (Pallets)\",\"Y (Time)\",\"XY\",\"X²\",\"Y²\"],\"rows\":[[\"1\",\"30\",\"20\",\"600\",\"900\",\"400\"],[\"2\",\"45\",\"27\",\"1215\",\"2025\",\"729\"],[\"3\",\"58\",\"35\",\"2030\",\"3364\",\"1225\"],[\"4\",\"65\",\"42\",\"2730\",\"4225\",\"1764\"],[\"5\",\"70\",\"58\",\"4060\",\"4900\",\"3364\"],[\"6\",\"85\",\"52\",\"4420\",\"7225\",\"2704\"],[\"7\",\"95\",\"76\",\"7220\",\"9025\",\"5776\"],[\"8\",\"98\",\"67\",\"6566\",\"9604\",\"4489\"],[\"SUM (n = 8)\",\"546\",\"377\",\"28,841\",\"41,268\",\"20,451\"]],\"type\":\"data-table\"},\"options\":[\"ŷ = 5.309 + 0.777x\",\"ŷ = 5.605 + 0.877x\",\"ŷ = −5.906 + 0.777x\",\"ŷ = −5.956x + 0.877\"],\"stem\":\"The table below gives pallet count and processing time for eight warehouse orders. What is the estimated regression equation for predicting processing time from pallet count?\",\"sub\":\"ana\",\"why\":\"x̄ = 546/8 = 68.25 and ȳ = 377/8 = 47.125. SSxy = ΣXY − nx̄ȳ = 28,841 − 8(68.25)(47.125) = 3,110.75, and SSxx = ΣX² − nx̄² = 41,268 − 8(68.25²) = 4,003.5. Thus b₁ = SSxy/SSxx = 0.777 and b₀ = ȳ − b₁x̄ = 47.125 − 0.777(68.25) = −5.906, giving ŷ = −5.906 + 0.777x. [VI.A.2]\"}","content":{"answer":2,"chart":{"columns":["Observation","X (Pallets)","Y (Time)","XY","X²","Y²"],"rows":[["1","30","20","600","900","400"],["2","45","27","1215","2025","729"],["3","58","35","2030","3364","1225"],["4","65","42","2730","4225","1764"],["5","70","58","4060","4900","3364"],["6","85","52","4420","7225","2704"],["7","95","76","7220","9025","5776"],["8","98","67","6566","9604","4489"],["SUM (n = 8)","546","377","28,841","41,268","20,451"]],"type":"data-table"},"options":["ŷ = 5.309 + 0.777x","ŷ = 5.605 + 0.877x","ŷ = −5.906 + 0.777x","ŷ = −5.956x + 0.877"],"stem":"The table below gives pallet count and processing time for eight warehouse orders. What is the estimated regression equation for predicting processing time from pallet count?","sub":"ana","why":"x̄ = 546/8 = 68.25 and ȳ = 377/8 = 47.125. SSxy = ΣXY − nx̄ȳ = 28,841 − 8(68.25)(47.125) = 3,110.75, and SSxx = ΣX² − nx̄² = 41,268 − 8(68.25²) = 4,003.5. Thus b₁ = SSxy/SSxx = 0.777 and b₀ = ȳ − b₁x̄ = 47.125 − 0.777(68.25) = −5.906, giving ŷ = −5.906 + 0.777x. [VI.A.2]"},"revision":"397a40f810fd60df6363c981714fa8983363808d26906479ea5c979a2e14cf09"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-412":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"chart\":{\"columns\":[\"Observation\",\"X (Pallets)\",\"Y (Time)\",\"XY\",\"X²\",\"Y²\"],\"rows\":[[\"1\",\"30\",\"20\",\"600\",\"900\",\"400\"],[\"2\",\"45\",\"27\",\"1215\",\"2025\",\"729\"],[\"3\",\"58\",\"35\",\"2030\",\"3364\",\"1225\"],[\"4\",\"65\",\"42\",\"2730\",\"4225\",\"1764\"],[\"5\",\"70\",\"58\",\"4060\",\"4900\",\"3364\"],[\"6\",\"85\",\"52\",\"4420\",\"7225\",\"2704\"],[\"7\",\"95\",\"76\",\"7220\",\"9025\",\"5776\"],[\"8\",\"98\",\"67\",\"6566\",\"9604\",\"4489\"],[\"SUM (n = 8)\",\"546\",\"377\",\"28,841\",\"41,268\",\"20,451\"]],\"type\":\"data-table\"},\"options\":[\"0.60\",\"0.70\",\"0.80\",\"0.90\"],\"stem\":\"Using the pallet-count and processing-time data shown below (SSxy = 3,110.75 and SSxx = 4,003.5), what is R², the coefficient of determination?\",\"sub\":\"ana\",\"why\":\"R² is the square of the correlation coefficient r. SSyy = ΣY² − nȳ² = 20,451 − 8(47.125²) = 2,684.875. Therefore, r = SSxy/√(SSxx × SSyy) = 3,110.75/√(4,003.5 × 2,684.875) = 0.9488, and R² = 0.9488² = 0.90. [VI.A.2]\"}","content":{"answer":3,"chart":{"columns":["Observation","X (Pallets)","Y (Time)","XY","X²","Y²"],"rows":[["1","30","20","600","900","400"],["2","45","27","1215","2025","729"],["3","58","35","2030","3364","1225"],["4","65","42","2730","4225","1764"],["5","70","58","4060","4900","3364"],["6","85","52","4420","7225","2704"],["7","95","76","7220","9025","5776"],["8","98","67","6566","9604","4489"],["SUM (n = 8)","546","377","28,841","41,268","20,451"]],"type":"data-table"},"options":["0.60","0.70","0.80","0.90"],"stem":"Using the pallet-count and processing-time data shown below (SSxy = 3,110.75 and SSxx = 4,003.5), what is R², the coefficient of determination?","sub":"ana","why":"R² is the square of the correlation coefficient r. SSyy = ΣY² − nȳ² = 20,451 − 8(47.125²) = 2,684.875. Therefore, r = SSxy/√(SSxx × SSyy) = 3,110.75/√(4,003.5 × 2,684.875) = 0.9488, and R² = 0.9488² = 0.90. [VI.A.2]"},"revision":"60f515a693860298e8cc70a6566e13bcb048241baec0fd071cd5570ac0aa658a"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-413":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"155.3\",\"230\",\"385.3\",\"456.8\"],\"stem\":\"A simple linear regression model predicts customer returns from the previous month''s sales: ŷ = 230 + 0.0034x. What is the expected number of returns if last month''s sales were 45,678 units?\",\"sub\":\"ana\",\"why\":\"Substitute x = 45,678 into the prediction equation: ŷ = 230 + 0.0034(45,678) = 385.3 expected returns. [VI.A.2]\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["155.3","230","385.3","456.8"],"stem":"A simple linear regression model predicts customer returns from the previous month''s sales: ŷ = 230 + 0.0034x. What is the expected number of returns if last month''s sales were 45,678 units?","sub":"ana","why":"Substitute x = 45,678 into the prediction equation: ŷ = 230 + 0.0034(45,678) = 385.3 expected returns. [VI.A.2]"},"revision":"b477fe792b726e2dd2cda51c7285226d78e1548234c08f4834c687ea228af159"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-414":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"Multiple linear regression model\",\"Nonlinear regression model\",\"Simple linear regression model\",\"Logistic regression model\"],\"stem\":\"A Black Belt estimates a regression model to be ŷ = −32.5 + 12.0x₁ + 0.45x₂ − 3.9x₁x₂. What type of model is this?\",\"sub\":\"ana\",\"why\":\"The equation ŷ = −32.5 + 12.0x₁ + 0.45x₂ − 3.9x₁x₂ is a multiple linear regression model because more than one independent variable predicts the response. [VI.A.3]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["Multiple linear regression model","Nonlinear regression model","Simple linear regression model","Logistic regression model"],"stem":"A Black Belt estimates a regression model to be ŷ = −32.5 + 12.0x₁ + 0.45x₂ − 3.9x₁x₂. What type of model is this?","sub":"ana","why":"The equation ŷ = −32.5 + 12.0x₁ + 0.45x₂ − 3.9x₁x₂ is a multiple linear regression model because more than one independent variable predicts the response. [VI.A.3]"},"revision":"8980d2a3eb9d09cca8c94b113580b9cba93b2992bf8977df88f8e6b089000df9"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-415":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"H₀: μ(start) = μ(end) versus H₁: μ(start) ≠ μ(end)\",\"H₀: μ(D) = 0 versus H₁: μ(D) is less than 0\",\"H₀: μ(D) ≠ 0 versus H₁: μ(D) = 0\",\"H₀: μ(D) = 0 versus H₁: μ(D) is greater than 0\"],\"stem\":\"To determine the efficacy of a weight-loss regimen, participants are weighed at the start and end of a 12-week program. Define D = starting weight − ending weight. Which hypotheses are appropriate for testing whether the program produces weight loss?\",\"sub\":\"ana\",\"why\":\"The same participants are measured twice, so this is a paired test. With D defined as starting weight minus ending weight, effective weight loss produces positive differences; therefore test H₀: μ(D) = 0 versus H₁: μ(D) is greater than 0. [VI.B.5]\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["H₀: μ(start) = μ(end) versus H₁: μ(start) ≠ μ(end)","H₀: μ(D) = 0 versus H₁: μ(D) is less than 0","H₀: μ(D) ≠ 0 versus H₁: μ(D) = 0","H₀: μ(D) = 0 versus H₁: μ(D) is greater than 0"],"stem":"To determine the efficacy of a weight-loss regimen, participants are weighed at the start and end of a 12-week program. Define D = starting weight − ending weight. Which hypotheses are appropriate for testing whether the program produces weight loss?","sub":"ana","why":"The same participants are measured twice, so this is a paired test. With D defined as starting weight minus ending weight, effective weight loss produces positive differences; therefore test H₀: μ(D) = 0 versus H₁: μ(D) is greater than 0. [VI.B.5]"},"revision":"708a254a79d7e619cd8ff1621c96a5ee64033525c1d99c98283f985c7416b204"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-416":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"Student''s t-test\",\"Fisher''s exact test\",\"Chi-square test\",\"ANOVA\"],\"stem\":\"To compare the means of three or more groups, which of the following tests is the most appropriate?\",\"sub\":\"ana\",\"why\":\"To compare the means of three or more groups, we use analysis of variance (ANOVA). [VI.B.6]\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["Student''s t-test","Fisher''s exact test","Chi-square test","ANOVA"],"stem":"To compare the means of three or more groups, which of the following tests is the most appropriate?","sub":"ana","why":"To compare the means of three or more groups, we use analysis of variance (ANOVA). [VI.B.6]"},"revision":"c038cceb89cbe8a87051e161d27cf0ae900c7e5f722a471aea4637217abe47d5"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-417":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"chart\":{\"columns\":[\"Source\",\"Sum of Squares\",\"df\",\"Mean Square\",\"F-statistic\"],\"rows\":[[\"Factor A\",\"144\",\"2\",\"\",\"\"],[\"Factor B\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\"],[\"AB Interaction\",\"360\",\"8\",\"\",\"\"],[\"Error\",\"75\",\"\",\"\",\"\"],[\"Total\",\"664\",\"29\",\"\",\"\"]],\"type\":\"data-table\"},\"options\":[\"2.13\",\"4.25\",\"9.0\",\"14.4\"],\"stem\":\"Using the partially completed two-way ANOVA table below, what is the F-statistic for Factor B?\",\"sub\":\"ana\",\"why\":\"First, df(A×B) = df(A) × df(B), so 8 = 2 × df(B) and df(B) = 4. Then df(error) = df(total) − df(A) − df(B) − df(A×B) = 29 − 2 − 4 − 8 = 15. SS(B) = SS(total) − SS(A) − SS(A×B) − SS(error) = 664 − 144 − 360 − 75 = 85. Thus MS(B) = 85/4 = 21.25, MS(error) = 75/15 = 5, and F(B) = 21.25/5 = 4.25. [VI.B.6]\"}","content":{"answer":1,"chart":{"columns":["Source","Sum of Squares","df","Mean Square","F-statistic"],"rows":[["Factor A","144","2","",""],["Factor B","","","",""],["AB Interaction","360","8","",""],["Error","75","","",""],["Total","664","29","",""]],"type":"data-table"},"options":["2.13","4.25","9.0","14.4"],"stem":"Using the partially completed two-way ANOVA table below, what is the F-statistic for Factor B?","sub":"ana","why":"First, df(A×B) = df(A) × df(B), so 8 = 2 × df(B) and df(B) = 4. Then df(error) = df(total) − df(A) − df(B) − df(A×B) = 29 − 2 − 4 − 8 = 15. SS(B) = SS(total) − SS(A) − SS(A×B) − SS(error) = 664 − 144 − 360 − 75 = 85. Thus MS(B) = 85/4 = 21.25, MS(error) = 75/15 = 5, and F(B) = 21.25/5 = 4.25. [VI.B.6]"},"revision":"52625f72afad1f3ae92c91c03facded2e01f9ce59014b6a2940620dfaf96509f"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-418":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"chart\":{\"columns\":[\"Source\",\"Sum of Squares\",\"df\",\"Mean Square\",\"F-statistic\"],\"rows\":[[\"Factor A\",\"144\",\"2\",\"\",\"\"],[\"Factor B\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"\"],[\"AB Interaction\",\"360\",\"8\",\"\",\"\"],[\"Error\",\"75\",\"\",\"\",\"\"],[\"Total\",\"664\",\"29\",\"\",\"\"]],\"type\":\"data-table\"},\"options\":[\"Factors A and B are significant.\",\"Factor A and the AB interaction are significant.\",\"Factor B and the AB interaction are significant.\",\"Factors A, B, and the AB interaction are significant.\"],\"stem\":\"Using the two-way ANOVA table below, which statement is correct at α = 0.05? Use critical F(2, 15) = 3.68, critical F(4, 15) = 3.06, and critical F(8, 15) = 2.64.\",\"sub\":\"ana\",\"why\":\"With df(error) = 15, Factor A is significant because F₀ = 14.4 > critical F(2, 15) = 3.68; Factor B is significant because F₀ = 4.25 > critical F(4, 15) = 3.06; and the A×B interaction is significant because F₀ = 9.0 > critical F(8, 15) = 2.64. All three are significant at α = 0.05. [VI.B.6]\"}","content":{"answer":3,"chart":{"columns":["Source","Sum of Squares","df","Mean Square","F-statistic"],"rows":[["Factor A","144","2","",""],["Factor B","","","",""],["AB Interaction","360","8","",""],["Error","75","","",""],["Total","664","29","",""]],"type":"data-table"},"options":["Factors A and B are significant.","Factor A and the AB interaction are significant.","Factor B and the AB interaction are significant.","Factors A, B, and the AB interaction are significant."],"stem":"Using the two-way ANOVA table below, which statement is correct at α = 0.05? Use critical F(2, 15) = 3.68, critical F(4, 15) = 3.06, and critical F(8, 15) = 2.64.","sub":"ana","why":"With df(error) = 15, Factor A is significant because F₀ = 14.4 > critical F(2, 15) = 3.68; Factor B is significant because F₀ = 4.25 > critical F(4, 15) = 3.06; and the A×B interaction is significant because F₀ = 9.0 > critical F(8, 15) = 2.64. All three are significant at α = 0.05. [VI.B.6]"},"revision":"3941f72b221c76ea3a0f8698569ef93b1c0f45a68158a4188725a4e32c67521d"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-419":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"chart\":{\"columns\":[\"Defect Type\",\"Length\",\"Weight\",\"Strength\"],\"rows\":[[\"Historical %\",\"50%\",\"25%\",\"25%\"],[\"Monthly Inspection\",\"60\",\"35\",\"45\"]],\"type\":\"data-table\"},\"options\":[\"The test statistic = 3.889 and the critical value = 5.991.\",\"The test statistic = 4.286 and the critical value = 5.991.\",\"The test statistic = 3.889 and the critical value = 7.815.\",\"The test statistic = 4.286 and the critical value = 7.815.\"],\"stem\":\"A Black Belt performs a chi-square goodness-of-fit test at α = 0.05 to determine whether last month''s defect distribution differs from historical percentages. For df = 2, use χ²crit = 5.991. Which statement is true?\",\"sub\":\"ana\",\"why\":\"The observed counts are 60, 35, and 45, for a total of 140. Historical percentages give expected counts of 70, 35, and 35. Thus χ² = (60 − 70)²/70 + (35 − 35)²/35 + (45 − 35)²/35 = 4.286. With 3 − 1 = 2 degrees of freedom, the α = 0.05 critical value is 5.991. [VI.B.7]\"}","content":{"answer":1,"chart":{"columns":["Defect Type","Length","Weight","Strength"],"rows":[["Historical %","50%","25%","25%"],["Monthly Inspection","60","35","45"]],"type":"data-table"},"options":["The test statistic = 3.889 and the critical value = 5.991.","The test statistic = 4.286 and the critical value = 5.991.","The test statistic = 3.889 and the critical value = 7.815.","The test statistic = 4.286 and the critical value = 7.815."],"stem":"A Black Belt performs a chi-square goodness-of-fit test at α = 0.05 to determine whether last month''s defect distribution differs from historical percentages. For df = 2, use χ²crit = 5.991. Which statement is true?","sub":"ana","why":"The observed counts are 60, 35, and 45, for a total of 140. Historical percentages give expected counts of 70, 35, and 35. Thus χ² = (60 − 70)²/70 + (35 − 35)²/35 + (45 − 35)²/35 = 4.286. With 3 − 1 = 2 degrees of freedom, the α = 0.05 critical value is 5.991. [VI.B.7]"},"revision":"a965f663a4716edf480f67ee56d69c3eb500fb851456e10f9a249e50ffc1b1fc"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-42":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"storming.\",\"performing.\",\"forming.\",\"norming.\"],\"stem\":\"The team phase in which team members begin to understand the need to operate as a team rather than as a group of individuals is referred to as:\",\"sub\":\"tm\",\"why\":\"During the norming stage, members begin to understand the need to operate as a team rather than as a group of individuals. [III.B.2]\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["storming.","performing.","forming.","norming."],"stem":"The team phase in which team members begin to understand the need to operate as a team rather than as a group of individuals is ref