ategic projects.","has the authority or ability to make changes to the process as required."],"stem":"The term White Belt is usually associated with an individual who:","sub":"p1","why":"White Belts have a basic understanding of Six Sigma principles. [I.B.1]"},"revision":"cd99bdecc6c68e0e24ead4464f7651c2e00945e45dfd9d6f13ac71e789acbc1e"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-564":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"appease the quality department.\",\"set the team up for failure.\",\"avoid suboptimizing the process.\",\"satisfy the project champion.\"],\"stem\":\"A Six Sigma project is chartered to speed up loan processing. The team tracks both processing time and error count. The error count was likely added to:\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"By simply concentrating on speed, the team may inadvertently create more process errors. Tracking both processing time and error counts will help the team avoid suboptimizing the process. [IV.B.5]\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["appease the quality department.","set the team up for failure.","avoid suboptimizing the process.","satisfy the project champion."],"stem":"A Six Sigma project is chartered to speed up loan processing. The team tracks both processing time and error count. The error count was likely added to:","sub":"def","why":"By simply concentrating on speed, the team may inadvertently create more process errors. Tracking both processing time and error counts will help the team avoid suboptimizing the process. [IV.B.5]"},"revision":"6bce6a826d4939b16cd67170f2ad283c80190a0c0e667c4a5be498306cc7fd2a"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-565":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"stakeholder.\",\"subject matter expert.\",\"Yellow Belt.\",\"project champion.\"],\"stem\":\"An employee who might experience negative effects from a Six Sigma project would be considered a:\",\"sub\":\"p2\",\"why\":\"An employee who might experience negative effects from a Six Sigma project would be considered a stakeholder. Stakeholders are those individuals or entities that will be affected by a project or can influence the outcome of the project. [II.A]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["stakeholder.","subject matter expert.","Yellow Belt.","project champion."],"stem":"An employee who might experience negative effects from a Six Sigma project would be considered a:","sub":"p2","why":"An employee who might experience negative effects from a Six Sigma project would be considered a stakeholder. Stakeholders are those individuals or entities that will be affected by a project or can influence the outcome of the project. [II.A]"},"revision":"02e80374382560caa7cdde93c3baf5ed4cba64dfb22cb0c5e3c85470f910fba2"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-566":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"SWOT.\",\"PDCA.\",\"DFSS.\",\"DFMEA.\"],\"stem\":\"A tool used in the design process to minimize or prevent failures and improve safety and quality is known as:\",\"sub\":\"ana\",\"why\":\"Design failure mode and effects analysis (DFMEA) is a tool used in the design process to minimize or prevent failures and improve safety and quality. [VI.C.2]\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["SWOT.","PDCA.","DFSS.","DFMEA."],"stem":"A tool used in the design process to minimize or prevent failures and improve safety and quality is known as:","sub":"ana","why":"Design failure mode and effects analysis (DFMEA) is a tool used in the design process to minimize or prevent failures and improve safety and quality. [VI.C.2]"},"revision":"aa98c803cdcade222c11cf4c5b34b0b1e84c459ee587411e25a3703d17275aef"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-567":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"tree diagram.\",\"prioritization matrix.\",\"scatter plot.\",\"project-scheduling tool.\"],\"stem\":\"A process decision program chart is a type of:\",\"sub\":\"def\",\"why\":\"A process decision program chart (PDPC) is a type of tree diagram. [IV.D.6]\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["tree diagram.","prioritization matrix.","scatter plot.","project-scheduling tool."],"stem":"A process decision program chart is a type of:","sub":"def","why":"A process decision program chart (PDPC) is a type of tree diagram. [IV.D.6]"},"revision":"47cb1ae39201317c8b7c13883d31f601d01f65aa383d1fb5e562f9d16e68b946"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-568":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"u-chart\",\"np-chart\",\"X̄-S chart\",\"c-chart\"],\"stem\":\"An auditor selects 25 financial reports each month and classifies them as complete or incomplete. Which control chart would be appropriate to monitor this process?\",\"sub\":\"con\",\"why\":\"An np-chart is used to track the number of defectives (failed units) in a sample when the sample size is constant over time. [VIII.A.4]\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["u-chart","np-chart","X̄-S chart","c-chart"],"stem":"An auditor selects 25 financial reports each month and classifies them as complete or incomplete. Which control chart would be appropriate to monitor this process?","sub":"con","why":"An np-chart is used to track the number of defectives (failed units) in a sample when the sample size is constant over time. [VIII.A.4]"},"revision":"8989d8d7fec4c5efb040eb147af9a75665b4dc0f46b98b8555a487afc3a805d5"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-569":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"80% of problems are due to 20% of the causes.\",\"3.4 defects per million opportunities.\",\"yield equal to 99.73%.\",\"RTY = 100%.\"],\"stem\":\"The statistical standard for quality associated with Six Sigma is:\",\"sub\":\"p1\",\"why\":\"The Six Sigma quality benchmark is 3.4 defects per million opportunities under the convention of a normally distributed six-sigma process with a long-term 1.5σ mean shift. [I.A.1]\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["80% of problems are due to 20% of the causes.","3.4 defects per million opportunities.","yield equal to 99.73%.","RTY = 100%."],"stem":"The statistical standard for quality associated with Six Sigma is:","sub":"p1","why":"The Six Sigma quality benchmark is 3.4 defects per million oppo