ric used by first-level managers to track progress and make decisions. [II.C.1]"},"revision":"343391bf8236f5ce58d414287959cde5c7b03f4af5005e40f8ec5c9ce9f40157"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-571":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"touch time.\",\"cycle time.\",\"takt time.\",\"throughput.\"],\"stem\":\"The time required to complete one unit from the beginning of the process to the end of the process is defined as:\",\"sub\":\"mea\",\"why\":\"Cycle time is the time required to complete one unit from the beginning of the process to the end of the process. [V.A.1]\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["touch time.","cycle time.","takt time.","throughput."],"stem":"The time required to complete one unit from the beginning of the process to the end of the process is defined as:","sub":"mea","why":"Cycle time is the time required to complete one unit from the beginning of the process to the end of the process. [V.A.1]"},"revision":"a88e5a8ab3126ca7d4200098e41372c5792b1a85f2dacbd8d3bfeabe6c736c5d"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-572":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"general factorial design.\",\"nested design.\",\"screening design.\",\"mixture design.\"],\"stem\":\"A winery conducts an experiment that varies the proportions of three varietals to create a new blend. The resulting blends are then graded on a tasting scale. The best experimental design for this situation is a:\",\"sub\":\"imp\",\"why\":\"When studying the effects of various percentages of ingredients, use a mixture design. These designs incorporate the dependency of the ingredient percentages in that they must sum to 100%. [VII.A.3]\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["general factorial design.","nested design.","screening design.","mixture design."],"stem":"A winery conducts an experiment that varies the proportions of three varietals to create a new blend. The resulting blends are then graded on a tasting scale. The best experimental design for this situation is a:","sub":"imp","why":"When studyi