ic, measurable, actionable, relevant, and time-bound. [IV.B.4]"},"revision":"e41f4f470d9a92a1278f8d61e931a2f1b7a79bc89b5c8e39a404bdcd49b0a966"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-640":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"predicts a future result before it occurs.\",\"is reported after the outcome has occurred and can no longer be changed.\",\"is always forward-looking.\",\"can only be operational.\"],\"stem\":\"A lagging indicator:\",\"sub\":\"p2\",\"why\":\"A lagging indicator measures an outcome after the fact. Leading indicators provide earlier warning and a chance to influence the result. [II.C.1]\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["predicts a future result before it occurs.","is reported after the outcome has occurred and can no longer be changed.","is always forward-looking.","can only be operational."],"stem":"A lagging indicator:","sub":"p2","why":"A lagging indicator measures an outcome after the fact. Leading indicators provide earlier warning and a chance to influence the result. [II.C.1]"},"revision":"f2e8f5f8df67809f41df2b5e4d5f5ea15011b24ef79e0d58436c27ba7b93cb10"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-641":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"chart\":{\"type\":\"vsm-symbol\"},\"options\":[\"Supermarket\",\"Production kanban\",\"Customer\",\"Safety or buffer stock\"],\"stem\":\"The symbol below is used on a value stream map to denote which of the following items?\",\"sub\":\"mea\",\"why\":\"This rectangle-with-a-cut-corner symbol denotes a production kanban in a value stream map. [V.A.2]\"}","content":{"answer":1,"chart":{"type":"vsm-symbol"},"options":["Supermarket","Production kanban","Customer","Safety or buffer stock"],"stem":"The symbol below is used on a value stream map to denote which of the following items?","sub":"mea","why":"This rectangle-with-a-cut-corner symbol denotes a production kanban in a value stream map. [V.A.2]"},"revision":"be3aa6da8728472a58a614da5a0b7150ed20b1fce126e11a2c6bf14622bb6b0d"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-642":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"0.50\",\"0.93\",\"30.0\",\"35.8\"],\"stem\":\"Average customer demand during a shift is 900 units. A shift is eight hours with staggered 30-minute lunch breaks during which the line continues running. There are two 15-minute maintenance breaks during which the line is shut down. What is the takt time in seconds per unit?\",\"sub\":\"mea\",\"why\":\"Only the two maintenance breaks reduce available production time because the line continues running during lunch. Takt time = [(480 − 15 − 15) × 60]/900 = 30.0 seconds per unit. [V.A.1]\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["0.50","0.93","30.0","35.8"],"stem":"Average customer demand during a shift is 900 units. A shift is eight hours with staggered 30-minute lunch breaks during which the line continues running. There are two 15-minute maintenance breaks during which the line is shut down. What is the takt time in seconds per unit?","sub":"mea","why":"Only the two maintenance breaks reduce available production time because the line continues running during lunch. Takt time = [(480 − 15 − 15) × 60]/900 = 30.0 seconds per unit. [V.A.1]"},"revision":"9c23b20a8e65f139f24866024e2c384a21d78a99053db8fa3a69a36ff4a7912b"},"cssbb:set-3:legacy-643":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"options\":[\"value stream analysis.\",\"gap analysis.\",\"SMART goal.\",\"key performance indicator.\"],\"stem\":\"A tool used to identify a performance difference between the current state and a desired future state is known as a:\",\"sub\":\"ana\",\"why\":\"Gap analysis is a tool used to identify a performance difference between the current and a desired future state using metrics implied by the states. [VI.D.1]\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["value stream analysis.","gap analysis.","SMART goal.","key performance indicator."],"stem":"A tool used to identify a performance difference between the current state and a desired future state is known as a:","sub":"ana","why":"Gap analysis is a tool used to identify a performance differe