ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A II. Define Phase, Question 23 (print p. 26), II.C.2.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"bokReference":"II.C.2","options":["Problem statement, purpose, cost projection, scope, and next steps","Scope, team member names, cost projection, benefits, and results","Vision statement, purpose, strategic plan, benefits, and results","Problem statement, purpose, benefits, scope, and resources needed"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":174,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":26,"sourceQuestion":23,"sourceSection":"II. Define Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A project charter should contain which elements?","sub":"cssgb-define","why":"Some charters may include cost numbers, but this is not a requirement. Focus on getting management and champion buy-in. Also note that some organizations use the A3 as their charters, which should have the same information on one page. <b>D. Problem statement, purpose, benefits, scope, and resources needed</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A II. Define Phase, Question 23 (print p. 26), II.C.2.</span>"},"revision":"6f97faf443daa91660fe14fbe506247f62a0bf1d702ef56880f003883de330c4"},"cssgb:set-2:source-175:1f5xhgp":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"bokReference\":\"II.C.3\",\"options\":[\"process decision program chart.\",\"affinity diagram.\",\"activity network diagram.\",\"Pareto chart.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter2.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":175,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":26,\"sourceQuestion\":24,\"sourceSection\":\"II. Define Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"A tool that can help refine the scope of a project is a(n):\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-define\",\"why\":\"A Pareto chart can help set the scope of a project by revealing the largest contributors to a problem. <b>D. Pareto chart.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A II. Define Phase, Question 24 (print p. 26), II.C.3.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"bokReference":"II.C.3","options":["process decision program chart.","affinity diagram.","activity network diagram.","Pareto chart."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":175,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":26,"sourceQuestion":24,"sourceSection":"II. Define Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A tool that can help refine the scope of a project is a(n):","sub":"cssgb-define","why":"A Pareto chart can help set the scope of a project by revealing the largest contributors to a problem. <b>D. Pareto chart.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A II. Define Phase, Question 24 (print p. 26), II.C.3.</span>"},"revision":"f02bdfa7dd1338195f083ad7d8eb83bc266386a434cad36a90ca32ebaef49371"},"cssgb:set-2:source-176:1f5xhgp":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"bokReference\":\"II.C.4\",\"options\":[\"by tracking only what management believes is important.\",\"tracking the data as early as possible to benchmark the current state.\",\"at the first milestone in order to get meaningful data.\",\"by selecting easy-to-collect measurements.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter2.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":176,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":26,\"sourceQuestion\":25,\"sourceSection\":\"II. Define Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"A key aspect of project metrics is to start:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-define\",\"why\":\"We should always aim to get as much data as possible prior to the official launch of a project. The Hawthorne Effect will skew the data if people realize they are being watched. <b>B. tracking the data as early as possible to benchmark the current state.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A II. Define Phase, Question 25 (print p. 26), II.C.4.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"bokReference":"II.C.4","options":["by tracking only what management believes is important.","tracking the data as early as possible to benchmark the current state.","at the first milestone in order to get meaningful data.","by selecting easy-to-collect measurements."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":176,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":26,"sourceQuestion":25,"sourceSection":"II. Define Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A key aspect of project metrics is to start:","sub":"cssgb-define","why":"We should always aim to get as much data as possible prior to the official launch of a project. The Hawthorne Effect will skew the data if people realize they are being watched. <b>B. tracking the data as early as possible to benchmark the current state.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A II. Define Phase, Question 25 (print p. 26), II.C.4.</span>"},"revision":"07f7615106e4888e90130b797f17750ba70994a9804edbdaec4852a1f3848b12"},"cssgb:set-2:source-177:1f5xhgp":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"bokReference\":\"II.C.5\",\"options\":[\"Gantt chart.\",\"affinity diagram.\",\"PERT chart.\",\"work breakdown.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter2.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":177,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":26,\"sourceQuestion\":26,\"sourceSection\":\"II. Define Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"A project planning tool that shows the early start, early finish, late start, and late finish times for each activity is known as a(n):\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-define\",\"why\":\"A PERT chart shows the early &amp; late start and early &amp; late finish times for each activity in the project plan. <b>C. PERT chart.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A II. Define Phase, Question 26 (print p. 26), II.C.5.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"bokReference":"II.C.5","options":["Gantt chart.","affinity diagram.","PERT chart.","work breakdown."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":177,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":26,"sourceQuestion":26,"sourceSection":"II. Define Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A project planning tool that shows the early start, early finish, late start, and late finish times for each activity is known as a(n):","sub":"cssgb-define","why":"A PERT chart shows the early &amp; late start and early &amp; late finish times for each activity in the project plan. <b>C. PERT chart.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A II. Define Phase, Question 26 (print p. 26), II.C.5.</span>"},"revision":"469db593349df4207d5d58d068c5f752a407534d7582c5ae815d8fd9b5539d40"},"cssgb:set-2:source-178:1f5xhgp":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"bokReference\":\"II.C.5\",\"chart\":{\"type\":\"wbs-diagram\"},\"options\":[\"activity network diagram.\",\"affinity diagram.\",\"force field analysis.\",\"work breakdown structure.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter2.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":178,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":27,\"sourceQuestion\":27,\"sourceSection\":\"II. Define Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"The following graphic is an example of a(n):\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-define\",\"why\":\"The figure below shows an example of a work breakdown structure. <b>D. work breakdown structure.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A II. Define Phase, Question 27 (print p. 27), II.C.5.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"bokReference":"II.C.5","chart":{"type":"wbs-diagram"},"options":["activity network diagram.","affinity diagram.","force field analysis.","work breakdown structure."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":178,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":27,"sourceQuestion":27,"sourceSection":"II. Define Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"The following graphic is an example of a(n):","sub":"cssgb-define","why":"The figure below shows an example of a work breakdown structure. <b>D. work breakdown structure.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A II. Define Phase, Question 27 (print p. 27), II.C.5.</span>"},"revision":"2d2361bba0f2770cb17963659f6e5b5dea29e7a1d13162cd3836dae5007344c2"},"cssgb:set-2:source-179:1f5xhgp":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"II.C.5\",\"options\":[\"The entire project will be delayed by 3 days.\",\"Activity B will no longer be on the critical path.\",\"The project will not be delayed if Activity A is completed early.\",\"Activity C will start 6 days late.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter2.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":179,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":27,\"sourceQuestion\":28,\"sourceSection\":\"II. Define Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"A Green Belt creates a PERT chart for a project. Activities B, C, and F are on the critical path. What is the result if Activity B is delayed by 3 days?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-define\",\"why\":\"Any delay in an activity on the critical path will result in a project delay. <b>A. The entire project will be delayed by 3 days.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A II. Define Phase, Question 28 (print p. 27), II.C.5.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"bokReference":"II.C.5","options":["The entire project will be delayed by 3 days.","Activity B will no longer be on the critical path.","The project will not be delayed if Activity A is completed early.","Activity C will start 6 days late."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":179,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":27,"sourceQuestion":28,"sourceSection":"II. Define Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A Green Belt creates a PERT chart for a project. Activities B, C, and F are on the critical path. What is the result if Activity B is delayed by 3 days?","sub":"cssgb-define","why":"Any delay in an activity on the critical path will result in a project delay. <b>A. The entire project will be delayed by 3 days.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A II. Define Phase, Question 28 (print p. 27), II.C.5.</span>"},"revision":"59c1f77bc5d467e5fada1ff0cece698606b0e8d6b4a9d90697f7fcca87411da3"},"cssgb:set-2:source-17:sebhe3":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"IV.B.2\",\"options\":[\"Chi-square\",\"Poisson\",\"Binomial\",\"Standard normal\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":17,\"sourcePart\":\"Part B: Practice Exam\",\"sourcePrintPage\":152,\"sourceQuestion\":17,\"sourceSection\":\"IV. Analyze Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book Practice Exam\",\"stem\":\"From which distribution does a confidence interval on the variance of a normal distribution use critical values?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-analyze\",\"why\":\"The chi-square distribution is used to test a standard deviation or variance from a normal distribution. <b>A. Chi-square</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 17 (print p. 152), IV.B.2.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"bokReference":"IV.B.2","options":["Ch