or team develops as many ideas concerning a topic as they can in a short period of time using various creativity techniques, it is called:","sub":"cssgb-define","why":"Brainstorming is a technique to elicit as many ideas as possible in a short period of time. <b>B. brainstorming.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 2 (print p. 149), II.F.3.</span>"},"revision":"87a5ee8a2d42cad092a2ab5daf663e7883edf771fb5287894f4f0d7dec734e59"},"cssgb:set-2:source-300:5m2iwb":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"III.E\",\"options\":[\"setting up an SPC process.\",\"conducting a DOE.\",\"developing control plans.\",\"preparing an FMEA.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":300,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":62,\"sourceQuestion\":74,\"sourceSection\":\"III. Measure Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"Conducting an MSA should be the first step in:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-measure\",\"why\":\"Conducting a measurement system analysis is a standard rule for using SPC. <b>A. setting up an SPC process.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 74 (print p. 62), III.E.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"bokReference":"III.E","options":["setting up an SPC process.","conducting a DOE.","developing control plans.","preparing an FMEA."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":300,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":62,"sourceQuestion":74,"sourceSection":"III. Measure Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"Conducting an MSA should be the first step in:","sub":"cssgb-measure","why":"Conducting a measurement system analysis is a standard rule for using SPC. <b>A. setting up an SPC process.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 74 (print p. 62), III.E.</span>"},"revision":"2e3048c49bc5570806a87f4299903a3c7acf712ba2063541b9803bfff8311edc"},"cssgb:set-2:source-301:5m2iwb":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"bokReference\":\"III.E\",\"options\":[\"Randomly picking parts from a production bin\",\"Picking consecutively produced parts from the process\",\"Finding rejected parts that will be scrapped\",\"Handpicking samples that cover the process spread\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":301,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":63,\"sourceQuestion\":75,\"sourceSection\":\"III. Measure Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"When selecting samples to use in an MSA study, which factor is the most important to a successful outcome?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-measure\",\"why\":\"Handpicking samples that cover the process spread is critical to ensure that you are identifying the correct process variation. In fact, ensuring sample parts that test the range of the gage is even better for looking at the gage variation. <b>D. Handpicking samples that cover the process spread</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 75 (print p. 63), III.E.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"bokReference":"III.E","options":["Randomly picking parts from a production bin","Picking consecutively produced parts from the process","Finding rejected parts that will be scrapped","Handpicking samples that cover the process spread"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":301,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":63,"sourceQuestion":75,"sourceSection":"III. Measure Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"When selecting samples to use in an MSA study, which factor is the most important to a successful outcome?","sub":"cssgb-measure","why":"Handpicking samples that cover the process spread is critical to ensure that you are identifying the correct process variation. In fact, ensuring sample parts that test the range of the gage is even better for looking at the gage variation. <b>D. Handpicking samples that cover the process spread</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 75 (print p. 63), III.E.</span>"},"revision":"8f0353eb549a8cb26aba221df725466dc18e6066c8a97bb958dd81566b79c7c5"},"cssgb:set-2:source-302:5m2iwb":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"bokReference\":\"III.E\",\"chart\":{\"columns\":[\"Appraiser / trial\",\"Part 1\",\"Part 2\",\"Part 3\",\"Part 4\",\"Part 5\"],\"rows\":[[\"A1\",\"23\",\"33\",\"22\",\"10\",\"15\"],[\"A2\",\"21\",\"31\",\"21\",\"10\",\"16\"],[\"A3\",\"19\",\"29\",\"23\",\"10\",\"11\"]],\"type\":\"data-table\"},\"options\":[\"18\",\"19\",\"20\",\"21\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":302,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":63,\"sourceQuestion\":76,\"sourceSection\":\"III. Measure Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"What is the rounded value for the overall average?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-measure\",\"why\":\"The three appraiser-trial averages are A1 = 20.6, A2 = 19.8, and A3 = 18.4. Their overall average is (20.6 + 19.8 + 18.4) / 3 = 19.6, which rounds to 20. <b>C. 20</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 76 (print p. 63), III.E.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"bokReference":"III.E","chart":{"columns":["Appraiser / trial","Part 1","Part 2","Part 3","Part 4","Part 5"],"rows":[["A1","23","33","22","10","15"],["A2","21","31","21","10","16"],["A3","19","29","23","10","11"]],"type":"data-table"},"options":["18","19","20","21"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":302,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":63,"sourceQuestion":76,"sourceSection":"III. Measure Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"What is the rounded value for the overall average?","sub":"cssgb-measure","why":"The three appraiser-trial averages are A1 = 20.6, A2 = 19.8, and A3 = 18.4. Their overall average is (20.6 + 19.8 + 18.4) / 3 = 19.6, which rounds to 20. <b>C. 20</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 76 (print p. 63), III.E.</span>"},"revision":"b6d9e3d5dcc637ce4bfa9009bd0d91046604109ebcb223284f679edddea4384c"},"cssgb:set-2:source-303:5m2iwb":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"III.E\",\"chart\":{\"columns\":[\"Appraiser / trial\",\"Part 1\",\"Part 2\",\"Part 3\",\"Part 4\",\"Part 5\"],\"rows\":[[\"A1\",\"23\",\"33\",\"22\",\"10\",\"15\"],[\"A2\",\"21\",\"31\",\"21\",\"10\",\"16\"],[\"A3\",\"19\",\"29\",\"23\",\"10\",\"11\"]],\"type\":\"data-table\"},\"options\":[\"21.0\",\"21.5\",\"22.0\",\"23.0\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":303,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":63,\"sourceQuestion\":77,\"sourceSection\":\"III. Measure Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"What is the value for R-bar?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-measure\",\"why\":\"Calculate the range for each row (A1 = 23, A2 = 21, A3 = 19) and then calculate the R-bar = 21. <b>A. 21.0</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 77 (print p. 63), III.E.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"bokReference":"III.E","chart":{"columns":["Appraiser / trial","Part 1","Part 2","Part 3","Part 4","Part 5"],"rows":[["A1","23","33","22","10","15"],["A2","21","31","21","10","16"],["A3","19",