ourcePrintPage\":155,\"sourceQuestion\":31,\"sourceSection\":\"V. Improve Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book Practice Exam\",\"stem\":\"Variables that show the observed results of an experimental treatment as a result of controlling levels, interactions, and a number of other factors are:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-improve\",\"why\":\"Response variables are the observed results of an experimental treatment. <b>B. response variables.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 31 (print p. 155), V.A.1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"bokReference":"V.A.1","options":["dependent variables.","response variables.","independent variables.","main effects."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":31,"sourcePart":"Part B: Practice Exam","sourcePrintPage":155,"sourceQuestion":31,"sourceSection":"V. Improve Phase","sourceType":"Book Practice Exam","stem":"Variables that show the observed results of an experimental treatment as a result of controlling levels, interactions, and a number of other factors are:","sub":"cssgb-improve","why":"Response variables are the observed results of an experimental treatment. <b>B. response variables.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 31 (print p. 155), V.A.1.</span>"},"revision":"a0b09fa60bba2e1ca408a274a6dd271b2088ae754cf344fbc6175a3fa2fd17ef"},"cssgb:set-2:source-320:5m2iwb":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"III.F.3\",\"options\":[\"Cp.\",\"X-bar.\",\"Pp.\",\"Ppk.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":320,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":67,\"sourceQuestion\":94,\"sourceSection\":\"III. Measure Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"The capability index calculated using the within-subgroup standard deviation is:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-measure\",\"why\":\"The Cp index is calculated using the within-subgroup standard deviation from a control chart. <b>A. Cp.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 94 (print p. 67), III.F.3.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"bokReference":"III.F.3","options":["Cp.","X-bar.","Pp.","Ppk."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":320,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":67,"sourceQuestion":94,"sourceSection":"III. Measure Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"The capability index calculated using the within-subgroup standard deviation is:","sub":"cssgb-measure","why":"The Cp index is calculated using the within-subgroup standard deviation from a control chart. <b>A. Cp.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 94 (print p. 67), III.F.3.</span>"},"revision":"ef20a054d0e157d56dfadb87722d368140ba8ad6c0442ddaae6d8f3ab4ad15ad"},"cssgb:set-2:source-321:5m2iwb":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"bokReference\":\"III.F.2\",\"options\":[\"A process with only short-term fluctuations\",\"A process with no historical data available\",\"A process with inconsistent variations\",\"A process producing a consistent output within specifications\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":321,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":67,\"sourceQuestion\":95,\"sourceSection\":\"III. Measure Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"Which process is best suited for interpreting process-capability measures as predictive of future performance?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-measure\",\"why\":\"Process-capability measures are predictive only after the process is stable, with consistent output and no unresolved special causes. The book keys inconsistent variation, but capability indices from an unstable process are not reliable predictors; the student-facing key is corrected here. <b>D. A process producing a consistent output within specifications</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 95 (print p. 67), III.F.2.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"bokReference":"III.F.2","options":["A process with only short-term fluctuations","A process with no historical data available","A process with inconsistent variations","A process producing a consistent output within specifications"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":321,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":67,"sourceQuestion":95,"sourceSection":"III. Measure Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"Which process is best suited for interpreting process-capability measures as predictive of future performance?","sub":"cssgb-measure","why":"Process-capability measures are predictive only after the process is stable, with consistent output and no unresolved special causes. The book keys inconsistent variation, but capability indices from an unstable process are not reliable predictors; the student-facing key is corrected here. <b>D. A process producing a consistent output within specifications</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 95 (print p. 67), III.F.2.</span>"},"revision":"886c1bc0b0890af5851c536c3abc7a691efc4311afe8df100b24a932a550c593"},"cssgb:set-2:source-322:5m2iwb":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"bokReference\":\"III.F.3\",\"options\":[\"Cp.\",\"Cpk.\",\"Pp.\",\"Ppk.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":322,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":67,\"sourceQuestion\":96,\"sourceSection\":\"III. Measure Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"The performance location of a nonstable process is denoted by:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-measure\",\"why\":\"Ppk is an index for unstable processes that indicates a general location within the specification limits. <b>D. Ppk.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 96 (print p. 67), III.F.3.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"bokReference":"III.F.3","options":["Cp.","Cpk.","Pp.","Ppk."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":322,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":67,"sourceQuestion":96,"sourceSection":"III. Measure Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"The performance location of a nonstable process is denoted by:","sub":"cssgb-measure","why":"Ppk is an index for unstable processes that indicates a general location within the specification limits. <b>D. Ppk.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 96 (print p. 67), III.F.3.</span>"},"revision":"7e03150302705eebd9a3f537f606f8fba0931af6c9d5c2e1e5efcbb5c434b070"},"cssgb:set-2:source-323:5m2iwb":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"bokReference\":\"III.F.3\",\"chart\":{\"columns\":[\"Parameter\",\"Value\"],\"rows\":[[\"Total sample size\",\"125\"],[\"Subgroup size\",\"5\"],[\"Number of subgroups\",\"25\"],[\"X̿\",\"0.52\"],[\"R̄\",\"0.66\"],[\"Overall sample standard deviation\",\"0.29\"],[\"LSL\",\"0\"],[\"USL\",\"2\"],[\"X̄-chart limits\",\"[0.13, 0.90]\"],[\"R-chart limits\",\"[0, 1.40]\"]],\"type\":\"data-table\"},\"options\":[\"0.60\",\"0.61\",\"1.11\",\"1.17\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":323,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":67,\"sourceQuestion\":97,\"sourceSection\":\"III. Measure Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"Estimate the value of Cp.\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-measure\",\"why\":\"Using the information from the control chart, we note that d₂ for n = 5 is equal to 2.326. Refer to Appendix E of The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Handbook. Then we estimate Cp: σ̂ = R̄/d₂ = 0.66/2.326; Cp = (2−0)/(6σ̂) = 1.17. <b>D. 1.17</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 97 (print p. 67), III.F.3.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"bokReference":"III.F.3","chart":{"columns":["Parameter","Value"],"rows":[["Total sample size","125"],["Subgroup size","5"],["Number of subgroups","25"],["X̿","0.52"],["R̄","0.66"],["Overall sample standard deviation","0.29"],["LSL","0"],["USL","2"],["X̄-chart limits","[0.13, 0.90]"],["R-chart limits","[0, 1.40]"]],"type":"data-table"},"options":["0.60","0.61","1.11","1.17"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":323,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":67,"sourceQuestion":97,"sourceSection":"III. Measure Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"Estimate the value of Cp.","sub":"cssgb-measure","why":"Using the information from the control chart, we note that d₂ for n = 5 is equal to 2.326. Refer to Appendix E of The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Handbook. Then we estimate Cp: σ̂ = R̄/d₂ = 0.66/2.326; Cp = (2−0)/(6σ̂) = 1.17. <b>D. 1.17</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 97 (print p. 67), III.F.3.</span>"},"revision":"3ab63ee696c1640c571012c9ca6a585abe6fb8d9f8f63b2944499ef6c631ecbc"},"cssgb:set-2:source-324:5m2iwb":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"bokReference\":\"III.F.3\",\"chart\":{\"columns\":[\"Parameter\",\"Value\"],\"rows\":[[\"Total sample size\",\"125\"],[\"Subgroup size\",\"5\"],[\"Number of subgroups\",\"25\"],[\"X̿\",\"0.52\"],[\"R̄\",\"0.66\"],[\