":69,\"sourceQuestion\":103,\"sourceSection\":\"III. Measure Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"A normally distributed process metric is currently running at a 3-sigma level of quality. What is the long-term yield of the process?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-measure\",\"why\":\"A 3-sigma level process indicates that the specifications of a normally distributed process distribution map to ± 3 standard deviations for the mean. The short-term yield is 99.73%. If we apply a 1.5 standard deviation shift in the mean, the long-term yield reduces to 93.32%. This can be determined using a chart that maps sigma level, to short and long-term DPMO and yield. <b>A. 93.32%</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 103 (print p. 69), III.F.4.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"bokReference":"III.F.4","options":["93.32%","95.45%","99.73%","99.99966%"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter3.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":329,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":69,"sourceQuestion":103,"sourceSection":"III. Measure Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A normally distributed process metric is currently running at a 3-sigma level of quality. What is the long-term yield of the process?","sub":"cssgb-measure","why":"A 3-sigma level process indicates that the specifications of a normally distributed process distribution map to ± 3 standard deviations for the mean. The short-term yield is 99.73%. If we apply a 1.5 standard deviation shift in the mean, the long-term yield reduces to 93.32%. This can be determined using a chart that maps sigma level, to short and long-term DPMO and yield. <b>A. 93.32%</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A III. Measure Phase, Question 103 (print p. 69), III.F.4.</span>"},"revision":"1a51bad15334d027a21c4eed76ad5fa2b57845d715f5633f7303782ad6ed5f33"},"cssgb:set-2:source-32:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"bokReference\":\"VI.B.3\",\"options\":[\"Survey from the training attendees with positive commentary\",\"Objective evidence of successful work from process changes and improvements\",\"Completion of third-party certifications in quality and Six Sigma management\",\"Subscription to online programs and webinars for continuity of additional training\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":32,\"sourcePart\":\"Part B: Practice Exam\",\"sourcePrintPage\":155,\"sourceQuestion\":32,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book Practice Exam\",\"stem\":\"How are training objectives proven to be successfully adopted and demonstrated?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"Training is not concluded until the imparted skills have been successfully adopted and demonstrated. This includes ongoing monitoring and verification of successful work completion, process adoption, and sustained improvements. <b>B. Objective evidence of successful work from process changes and improvements</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 32 (print p. 155), VI.B.3.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"bokReference":"VI.B.3","options":["Survey from the training attendees with positive commentary","Objective evidence of successful work from process changes and improvements","Completion of third-party certifications in quality and Six Sigma management","Subscription to online programs and webinars for continuity of additional training"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":32,"sourcePart":"Part B: Practice Exam","sourcePrintPage":155,"sourceQuestion":32,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book Practice Exam","stem":"How are training objectives proven to be successfully adopted and demonstrated?","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"Training is not concluded until the imparted skills have been successfully adopted and demonstrated. This includes ongoing monitoring and verification of successful work completion, process adoption, and sustained improvements. <b>B. Objective evidence of successful work from process changes and improvements</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 32 (print p. 155), VI.B.3.</span>"},"revision":"d43d78b8735e7a52eae701304574fc3050b3b00e2c5e7234f7b0e14ee7fb23a6"},"cssgb:set-2:source-330:sebhe3":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"bokReference\":\"IV.A.1\",\"options\":[\"Average, spread, and location\",\"Skewness and kurtosis\",\"Cyclical, temporal, and positional\",\"Thermal and geographic placement\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter4.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":330,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":82,\"sourceQuestion\":1,\"sourceSection\":\"IV. Analyze Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"The multi-vari chart is a useful tool for analyzing what types of variation?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-analyze\",\"why\":\"The multi-vari chart is a useful tool for analyzing cyclical, temporal, and positional variation. <b>C. Cyclical, temporal, and positional</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A IV. Analyze Phase, Question 1 (print p. 82), IV.A.1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"bokReference":"IV.A.1","options":["Average, spread, and location","Skewness and kurtosis","Cyclical, temporal, and positional","Thermal and geographic placement"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter4.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":330,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":82,"sourceQuestion":1,"sourceSection":"IV. Analyze Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"The multi-vari chart is a useful tool for analyzing what types of variation?","sub