 82), IV.A.1.</span>"},"revision":"193eea3d3e3283a49061a0dcc6402f3ecf95cb7296eeca95ffb71b19c80894e0"},"cssgb:set-2:source-332:sebhe3":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"bokReference\":\"IV.A.1\",\"options\":[\"Create a value stream process flow map of the target area.\",\"Select the process and the characteristics to be investigated.\",\"Record the time and values from each sample set in a table format.\",\"Use a cross-functional team to conduct a root cause analysis of the target area.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter4.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":332,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":82,\"sourceQuestion\":3,\"sourceSection\":\"IV. Analyze Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"When developing a multi-vari sampling plan, what should be the first step?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-analyze\",\"why\":\"The first step when developing a multi-vari sampling plan is to select the process and the characteristics to be investigated. <b>B. Select the process and the characteristics to be investigated.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A IV. Analyze Phase, Question 3 (print p. 82), IV.A.1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"bokReference":"IV.A.1","options":["Create a value stream process flow map of the target area.","Select the process and the characteristics to be investigated.","Record the time and values from each sample set in a table format.","Use a cross-functional team to conduct a root cause analysis of the target area."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter4.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":332,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":82,"sourceQuestion":3,"sourceSection":"IV. Analyze Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"When developing a multi-vari sampling plan, what should be the first step?","sub":"cssgb-analyze","why":"The first step when developing a multi-vari sampling plan is to 