tem\":\"What is the interpretation of slope in a simple linear regression?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-analyze\",\"why\":\"The interpretation of the slope is that if x increases by 1 unit, ŷ will change by the amount of the slope. <b>B. If x increases by 1 unit, ŷ will change by the amount of the slope.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A IV. Analyze Phase, Question 18 (print p. 87), IV.A.2.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"bokReference":"IV.A.2","options":["If ŷ increases by 1 unit, x will increase by the amount of the slope.","If x increases by 1 unit, ŷ will change by the amount of the slope.","If x equals 0, ŷ will equal the slope.","An increase in x will cause ŷ to increase."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter4.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":347,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":87,"sourceQuestion":18,"sourceSection":"IV. Analyze Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"What is the interpretation of slope in a simple linear regression?","sub":"cssgb-analyze","why":"The interpretation of the slope is that if x increases by 1 unit, ŷ will change by the amount of the slope. <b>B. If x increases by 1 unit, ŷ will change by the amount of the slope.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A IV. Analyze Phase, Question 18 (print p. 87), IV.A.2.</span>"},"revision":"26385c064a8c44c61a1d4979f8f5c92888a907aec77a0860e5e894b4b24628f3"},"cssgb:set-2:source-348:sebhe3":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"bokReference\":\"IV.A.2\",\"options\":[\"$357.50\",\"$1246.55\",\"$1250.00\",\"$1253.45\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter4.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":348,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":87,\"sourceQuestion\":19,\"sourceSection\":\"IV. Analyze Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"A simple linear regression model was estimated to predict the shipping cost for an item based on the number of units: ŷ = −3.45 + 12.5x. What is the expected shipping cost for 100 units?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-analyze\",\"why\":\"Using the simple linear regression equation, we calculate: ŷ = −3.45 + 12.5(100) = 1246.55. <b>B. $1246.55</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A IV. Analyze Phase, Question 19 (print p. 87), IV.A.2.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"bokReference":"IV.A.2","options":["$357.50","$1246.55","$1250.00","$1253.45"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter4.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":348,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":87,"sourceQuestion":19,"sourceSection":"IV. Analyze Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A simple linear regression model was estimated to predict the shipping cost for an item based on the number of units: ŷ = −3.45 + 12.5x. What is the expected shipping cost for 100 units?","sub":"cssgb-analyze","why":"Using the simple linear regression equation, we calculate: ŷ = −3.45 + 12.5(100) = 1246.55. <b>B. $1246.55</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A IV. Analyze Phase, Question 19 (print p. 87), IV.A.2.</span>"},"revision":"cbab5d02150696c54ffcd432326b7109f21725c20b2e8b5de12c7cba5944ec48"},"cssgb:set-2:source-349:sebhe3":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"IV.A.2\",\"options\":[\"the y-intercept.\",\"the slope.\",\"the dependent variable.\",\"the independent variable.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter4.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":349,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":87,\"sourceQuestion\":20,\"sourceSection\":\"IV. Analyze Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"For the fitted regression model ŷ = −12.45 + 2.75x, the value –12.45 represents:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-analyze\",\"why\":\"The value –12.45 is the y-intercept of the regression line. <b>A. the y-intercept.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A IV. Analyze Phase, Question 20 (print p. 87), IV.A.2.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"bokReference":"IV.A.2","options":["the y-intercept.","the slope.","the dependent variable.","the independent variable."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter4.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":349,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":87,"sourceQuestion":20,"sourceSection":"IV. Analyze Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"For the fitted regression model ŷ = −12.45 + 2.75x, the value –12.45 represents:","sub":"cssgb-analyze","why":"The value –12.45 is the y-intercept of the regression line. <b>A. the y-intercept.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A IV. Analyze Phase, Question 20 (print p. 87), IV.A.2.</span>"},"revision":"6c40e7b845a450bdc6629a2ec8d9799296e21d07bc1c0af304a8ff35e91fb755"},"cssgb:set-2:source-34:5m2iwb":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"III.C\",\"options\":[\"0.82%\",\"40.52%\",\"59.48%\",\"99.18%\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":34,\"sourcePart\":\"Part B: Practice Exam\",\"sourcePrintPage\":156,\"sourceQuestion\":34,\"sourceSection\":\"III. Measure Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book Practice Exam\",\"stem\":\"The weight of soup cans follows a normal distribution with a mean of 16.0 oz and a standard deviation of 0.005 oz. What percentage of cans weigh more than 16.012 oz?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-measure\",\"why\":\"The standardized value is z = (16.012−16.000)/0.005 = 2.4. The upper-tail probability is P(Z &gt; 2.4) = 0.0082, or 0.82%. <b>A. 0.82%</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 34 (print p. 156), III.C.</span>\"}","content":