. Analyze Phase, Question 66 (print p. 97), IV.C.2.</span>"},"revision":"e81e4e91bc7ac125345466bb8950f56a9b2cdb8ecf4eb6d2b14f486ba4f531e0"},"cssgb:set-2:source-396:sebhe3":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"bokReference\":\"IV.C.2\",\"options\":[\"problems or goals.\",\"categories of possible causes.\",\"defect rates.\",\"individual workers.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter4.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":396,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":98,\"sourceQuestion\":67,\"sourceSection\":\"IV. Analyze Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"The labels on the main bones of a cause-and-effect diagram refer to:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-analyze\",\"why\":\"In a cause-and-effect, or fishbone, diagram, the main bones are labeled with categories of possible causes of the problem. <b>B. categories of possible causes.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A IV. Analyze Phase, Question 67 (print p. 98), IV.C.2.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"bokReference":"IV.C.2","options":["problems or goals.","categories of possible causes.","defect rates.","individual workers."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter4.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":396,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":98,"sourceQuestion":67,"sourceSection":"IV. Analyze Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"The labels on the main bones of a cause-and-effect diagram refer to:","sub":"cssgb-analyze","why":"In a cause-and-effect, or fishbone, diagram, the main bones are labeled with categories of possible causes of the problem. <b>B. categories of possible causes.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A IV. Analyze Phase, Question 67 (print p. 98), IV.C.2.</span>"},"revision":"200a20e37a13e0384d07b6130ebb1bd3edb369ce794b71943b3609cacfbf8f99"},"cssgb:set-2:source-397:sebhe3":{