, Part B Practice Exam, Question 40 (print p. 157), V.A.1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"bokReference":"V.A.1","options":["make the experiment harder to conduct.","separate the runs into blocks.","reduce interactions of the factors.","minimize the effect of uncontrolled variables."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":40,"sourcePart":"Part B: Practice Exam","sourcePrintPage":157,"sourceQuestion":40,"sourceSection":"V. Improve Phase","sourceType":"Book Practice Exam","stem":"The purpose of randomizing the order of experimental runs is to:","sub":"cssgb-improve","why":"Randomizing the order of the experimental runs will minimize the effect of uncontrolled variables on the response, thus increasing the statistical validity of the results. <b>D. minimize the effect of uncontrolled variables.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 40 (print p. 157), V.A.1.</span>"},"revision":"2572089d192674c2279fac7c7308904bee7625634c7789509cbaea25ad0ffb20"},"cssgb:set-2:source-410:1up69ca":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"bokReference\":\"V.A.1\",\"options\":[\"responses for each run.\",\"factors varied in the experiment.\",\"experimental error.\",\"experimental effect.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter5.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":410,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":111,\"sourceQuestion\":10,\"sourceSection\":\"V. Improve Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"In an experiment, the independent variables represent the:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-improve\",\"why\":\"The independent variables are the factors that are varied in the experiment. <b>B. factors varied in the experiment.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A V. Improve Phase, Question 10 (print p. 111), V.A.1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"bokReference":