y runs?","sub":"cssgb-improve","why":"A 3² experiment has two factors varied at three levels each. The minimum number of runs for this experiment is 9. <b>C. 9</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A V. Improve Phase, Question 12 (print p. 112), V.A.1.</span>"},"revision":"a719f55138aca26ccda02756ce133054f0e13f67d4895e960280ee58bf49b712"},"cssgb:set-2:source-413:1up69ca":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"bokReference\":\"V.A.1\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"8\",\"16\",\"32\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter5.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":413,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":112,\"sourceQuestion\":13,\"sourceSection\":\"V. Improve Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"A half-fraction of a 2⁵ experiment has how many runs?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-improve\",\"why\":\"A half-fraction of a 2⁵ experiment has 2⁵⁻¹ = 2⁴ = 16 runs. <b>C. 16</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A V. Improve Phase, Question 13 (print p. 112), V.A.1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"bokReference":"V.A.1","options":["5","8","16","32"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter5.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":413,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":112,"sourceQuestion":13,"sourceSection":"V. Improve Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A half-fraction of a 2⁵ experiment has how many runs?","sub":"cssgb-improve","why":"A half-fraction of a 2⁵ experiment has 2⁵⁻¹ = 2⁴ = 16 runs. <b>C. 16</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A V. Improve Phase, Question 13 (print p. 112), V.A.1.</span>"},"revision":"013528c753edb8c021e7dad9c59d2f261a71f07e011c0012bb014d3d0831588f"},"cssgb:set-2:source-414:1up69ca":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"V.A.1\",\"options\":[\"experimental obje