rove Phase, Question 21 (print p. 115), V.A.2.</span>"},"revision":"ce43d15cc4d3f58586977a89341f965067bfbdf3e524b68e12aa144b6b7bb2e3"},"cssgb:set-2:source-422:1up69ca":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"V.B\",\"options\":[\"proof of concept.\",\"try-storming simulations.\",\"pilot test.\",\"advanced product quality planning.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter5.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":422,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":115,\"sourceQuestion\":22,\"sourceSection\":\"V. Improve Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"A technique used in early-stage design validation that confirms the feasibility of the initiative and presents it to the participants and stakeholders for the purpose of eliciting feedback and detailed inputs is called:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-improve\",\"why\":\"Proof of concept is an early-stage design validation technique that confirms the feasibility of the initiative. This is presented to the participants and stakeholders for eliciting feedback and detailed inputs. <b>A. proof of concept.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A V. Improve Phase, Question 22 (print p. 115), V.B.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"bokReference":"V.B","options":["proof of concept.","try-storming simulations.","pilot test.","advanced product quality planning."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter5.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":422,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":115,"sourceQuestion":22,"sourceSection":"V. Improve Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A technique used in early-stage design validation that confirms the feasibility of the initiative and presents it to the participants and stakeholders for the purpose of eliciting feedback and detailed inputs is called:","sub":"cssgb-improve","why":"Proof of concept is an early-stage design validation technique that confirms the feasibility of the initiative. This is presented to the participants and stakeholders for eliciting feedback and detailed inputs. <b>A. proof of concept.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A V. Improve Phase, Question 22 (print p. 115), V.B.</span>"},"revision":"b2cfb429d3ba25fba65e3ec3570034ac4dbd93be74cdfab85ddf12403302689c"},"cssgb:set-2:source-423:1up69ca":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"V.B\",\"options\":[\"quickly simulate the most promising brainstorming ideas.\",\"move a Six Sigma team from the storming to norming stage.\",\"verify the effectiveness of the process solution.\",\"demonstrate that success criteria can be fulfilled.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter5.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":423,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":116,\"sourceQuestion\":23,\"sourceSection\":\"V. Improve Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"Try-storming is a technique that aims to:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-improve\",\"why\":\"Try-storming is a technique that aims to quickly simulate the most promising brainstormed ideas. <b>A. quickly simulate the most promising brainstorming ideas.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A V. Improve Phase, Question 23 (print p. 116), V.B.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"bokReference":"V.B","options":["quickly simulate the most promising brainstorming ideas.","move a Six Sigma team from the storming to norming stage.","verify the effectiveness of the process solution.","demonstrate that success criteria can be fulfilled."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter5.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":423,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":116,"sourceQuestion":23,"sourceSection":"V. Improve Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"Try-storming is a technique that aims to:","sub":"cssgb-improve","why":"Try-storming is a technique that aims to quickly simulate the most promising brainstormed ideas. <b>A. quickly simulate the most promising brainstorming ideas.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A V. Improve Phase, Question 23 (print p. 116), V.B.</span>"},"revision":"c72ae41c6d2636bb6bfac08c0fcf1c70df4c56d4988f2ff60b09fcf16e4cec9e"},"cssgb:set-2:source-424:1up69ca":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"bokReference\":\"V.B\",\"options\":[\"proof of concept.\",\"try-storming simulations.\",\"pilot testing.\",\"advanced product quality planning.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter5.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":424,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":116,\"sourceQuestion\":24,\"sourceSection\":\"V. Improve Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"A process that allows the team to sample the solution prior to completion is called:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-improve\",\"why\":\"Pilot testing lets the team try and refine a proposed solution on a limited scale before full deployment. <b>C. pilot testing.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A V. Improve Phase, Question 24 (print p. 116), V.B.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"bokReference":"V.B","options":["proof of concept.","try-storming simulations.","pilot testing.","advanced product quality planning."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter5.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":424,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":116,"sourceQuestion":24,"sourceSection":"V. Improve Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A process that allows the team to sample the solution prior to completion is called:","sub":"cssgb-improve","why":"Pilot testing lets the team try and refine a proposed solution on a limited scale before full deployment. <b>C. pilot testing.<