bjective is to:","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"Choose subgroups to minimize piece-to-piece variation. <b>A. minimize piece-to-piece variation within the subgroup.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 7 (print p. 127), VI.A.2.</span>"},"revision":"bc235360ec87a8bf422ac081b05c5d2957ff92dd4e2fa2be6b8a3ae92471ba8d"},"cssgb:set-2:source-452:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"VI.A.2\",\"options\":[\"Rational subgrouping will have to be considered.\",\"The tensile strength must be converted to pass/fail data.\",\"The specifications for tensile strength will have to be adjusted.\",\"No changes will be needed.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":452,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":127,\"sourceQuestion\":8,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"Pieces from five spot-welding stations flow onto a common conveyor belt. An operator chooses five consecutive pieces each hour to test the tensile strength of the welds. How might this procedure change once an X-bar R chart is used to track the tensile strength?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"Rational sub-grouping will have to be considered. Now, samples are a mixture of pieces from five different stations. <b>A. Rational subgrouping will have to be considered.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 8 (print p. 127), VI.A.2.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"bokReference":"VI.A.2","options":["Rational subgrouping will have to be considered.","The tensile strength must be converted to pass/fail data.","The specifications for tensile strength will have to be adjusted.","No changes will be needed."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":452,"sou