chart","np chart","c-chart"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":454,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":128,"sourceQuestion":10,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A control chart will be created to monitor a process with an automated vision system to measure height, the critical feature. A subgroup size of 15 will be used. Which of the following control charts is best suited for this application?","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"Use an X-bar and S chart when measuring continuous variables with subgroup sizes greater than or equal to 10. <b>B. X-bar and S chart</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 10 (print p. 128), VI.A.3.</span>"},"revision":"a991d2629780cdbf07be0199168fd31672310a46c469cb457ed43fc913607703"},"cssgb:set-2:source-455:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"bokReference\":\"VI.A.3\",\"options\":[\"p\",\"np\",\"XmR\",\"c\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":455,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":128,\"sourceQuestion\":11,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"A powder coating line will be monitored for quality. The number of defects per item will be counted using a constant sample size. Which of the following control charts is best suited for this application?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"Use a c-chart when counting defects per sampling unit with a constant sample size. <b>D. c</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 11 (print p. 128), VI.A.3.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"bokReference":"VI.A.3","options":["p","np","XmR","c"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":455,"sou