\"25\"],[\"Constant subgroup size, n\",\"200\"]],\"type\":\"data-table\"},\"options\":[\"[0, 1.30]\",\"[0, 7.26]\",\"[0, 8.38]\",\"[2.46, 3.78]\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":470,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":131,\"sourceQuestion\":26,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"What are the upper and lower control limits of the np-chart?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"To calculate the control limits of the np-chart, we first must find p-bar: p̄ = 78/(25×200) = 0.0156. Then, np-chart limits = np̄ ± 3√[np̄(1−p̄)] = [0, 8.38]. <b>C. [0, 8.38]</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 26 (print p. 131), VI.A.3.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"bokReference":"VI.A.3","chart":{"columns":["Parameter","Value"],"rows":[["Total nonconforming, Σnp","78"],["Number of subgroups, k","25"],["Constant subgroup size, n","200"]],"type":"data-table"},"options":["[0, 1.30]","[0, 7.26]","[0, 8.38]","[2.46, 3.78]"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":470,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":131,"sourceQuestion":26,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"What are the upper and lower control limits of the np-chart?","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"To calculate the control limits of the np-chart, we first must find p-bar: p̄ = 78/(25×200) = 0.0156. Then, np-chart limits = np̄ ± 3√[np̄(1−p̄)] = [0, 8.38]. <b>C. [0, 8.38]</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 26 (print p. 131), VI.A.3.</span>"},"revision":"e73baa73bacb2027406a49fd6165eff50735308a8f9070be21829bbc7a4cc520"},"cssgb:set-2:source-471:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"bokReference\":\