. 132), VI.B.1.</span>"},"revision":"cc0f4f678e23ed97cf307d605581a563c6110c15b1cebe7bf383d1111abe6be7"},"cssgb:set-2:source-476:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"bokReference\":\"VI.B.1\",\"options\":[\"implement validations on specific processes.\",\"ensure that process changes are maintained over time.\",\"create a structure for implementing quality throughout the process.\",\"keep only one item as a variable and maintain all other characteristics as controls per experiment.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":476,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":132,\"sourceQuestion\":32,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"The primary purpose of the control plan is to:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"The primary purpose of a control plan is to ensure that process changes are maintained over time. <b>B. ensure that process changes are maintained over time.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 32 (print p. 132), VI.B.1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"bokReference":"VI.B.1","options":["implement validations on specific processes.","ensure that process changes are maintained over time.","create a structure for implementing quality throughout the process.","keep only one item as a variable and maintain all other characteristics as controls per experiment."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":476,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":132,"sourceQuestion":32,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"The primary purpose of the control plan is to:","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"The primary purpose of a control plan is to ensure that process changes are maintained over time. <b>B. ensure that process changes are maintained over time.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 32 (print p. 132), VI.B.1.</span>"},"revision":"fb5a6f1f7479abe3736e70050e006fa79fb98057c135076cf4b104baf9514f20"},"cssgb:set-2:source-477:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"bokReference\":\"VI.B.1\",\"options\":[\"the paperwork burden remains high.\",\"internal auditors are kept busy.\",\"improvements are sustained over time.\",\"the right people get credit for the improvement.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":477,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":133,\"sourceQuestion\":33,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"Developing documents such as SOPs, work instructions, and control plans helps ensure that:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"Developing documents such as SOPs, work instructions, and control plans help ensure that improvements are sustained over time. <b>C. improvements are sustained over time.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 33 (print p. 133), VI.B.1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"bokReference":"VI.B.1","options":["the paperwork burden remains high.","internal auditors are kept busy.","improvements are sustained over time.","the right people get credit for the improvement."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":477,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":133,"sourceQuestion":33,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"Developing documents such as SOPs, work instructions, and control plans helps ensure that:","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"Developing documents such as SOPs, work instructions, and control plans help ensure that improvements are sustained over time. <b>C. improvements are sustained over time.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 33 (print p. 133), VI.B.1.</span>"},"revision":"a81901ab47b57de803899cf3452ce7fb30475aac58b54966afed0a8be3d85933"},"cssgb:set-2:source-478:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"bokReference\":\"VI.B.1\",\"options\":[\"SOPs\",\"Control charts\",\"Gage R&R\",\"Control plan\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":478,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":133,\"sourceQuestion\":34,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"Which of the following tools is used to monitor a process to ensure that the process improvements are continuing to produce the desired results?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"Control charts are used to monitor a process and make sure that improvements continue to produce the desired results. <b>B. Control charts</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 34 (print p. 133), VI.B.1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"bokReference":"VI.B.1","options":["SOPs","Control charts","Gage R&R","Control plan"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":478,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":133,"sourceQuestion":34,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"Which of the following tools is used to monitor a process to ensure that the process improvements are continuing to produce the desired results?","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"Control charts are used to monitor a process and make sure that improvements continue to produce the desired results. <b>B. Control charts</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 34 (print p. 133), VI.B.1.</span>"},"revision":"289a5802ec7165343c6ace0dad0de18b22dd763a8b88b0519a683c6872cb5987"},"cssgb:set-2:source-479:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"VI.B.1\",\"options\":[\"reduce process variation.\",\"allow for gradual improvement over time.\",\"aid in benchmarking efforts.\",\"create an atmosphere of mistrust.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":479,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":133,\"sourceQuestion\":35,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"Standard operating procedures (SOPs) and work instructions can:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"SOPs and work instructions help ensure that procedures are performed the same way each time, which reduces process variation. <b>A. reduce process variation.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 35 (print p. 133), VI.B.1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"bokReference":"VI.B.1","options":["reduce process variation.","allow for gradual improvement over time.","aid in benchmarking efforts.","create an atmosphere of mistrust."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":479,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":133,"sourceQuestion":35,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"Standard operating procedures (SOPs) and work instructions can:","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"SOPs and work instructions help ensure that procedures are performed the same way each time, which reduces process variation. <b>A. reduce process variation.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 35 (print p. 133), VI.B.1.</span>"},"revision":"edfdc805ae5830ab41b7b53ed7b59781da3b66549f2cc375b7cdca6544168f21"},"cssgb:set-2:source-47:10hzvwm":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"bokReference\":\"I.B.1\",\"options\":[\"the manufacturer recognizes the value, it lowers the cost of the product, and it is done right the first time.\",\"exceptional design teams have been developed, the product is transformed, and it is made faster than ever before.\",\"the customer recognizes the value, it changes (transforms) the product, and it is done right the first time.\",\"the customer recognizes the value, the industry is globally transformed, and there are no gray areas between value and non-value.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":47,\"sourcePart\":\"Part B: Practice Exam\",\"sourcePrintPage\":158,\"sourceQuestion\":47,\"sourceSection\":\"I. Six Sigma and the Organization\",\"sourceType\":\"Book Practice Exam\",\"stem\":\"Lean experts define a process step as value-added if:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-org\",\"why\":\"Lean focuses on the value given to the customer versus the value given to your organization. <b>C. the customer recognizes the value, it changes (transforms) the product, and it is done right the first time.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 47 (print p. 158), I.B.1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"bokReference":"I.B.1","options":["the manufacturer recognizes the value, it lowers the cost of the product, and it is done right the first time.","exceptional design teams have been developed, the product is transformed, and it is made faster than ever before.","the customer recognizes the value, it changes (transforms) the product, and it is done right the first time.","the customer recognizes the value, the industry is globally transformed, and there are no gray areas between value and non-value."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":47,"sourcePart":"Part B: Practice Exam","sourcePrintPage":158,"sourceQuestion":47,"sourceSection":"I. Six Sigma and the Organization","sourceType":"Book Practice Exam","stem":"Lean experts define a process step as value-added if:","sub":"cssgb-org","why":"Lean focuses on the value given to the customer versus the value given to your organization. <b>C. the customer recognizes the value, it changes (transforms) the product, and it is done right the first time.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 47 (print p. 158), I.B.1.</span>"},"revision":"8ee83b715fe613df7a31b22078d5c2f5fa18a508606325d90045f4452925e6e3"},"cssgb:set-2:source-480:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"bokReference\":\"VI.B.2\",\"options\":[\"document control practices are suspended during operations.\",\"standard operating procedures, failure modes, and effects analysis contradict each other.\",\"root causes and corrective actions are applied to future versions.\",\"Identify the update and route it through the approved document-control review.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":480,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":133,\"sourceQuestion\":36,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"A dynamic control plan is a living document. How should operators handle a needed update when process conditions change?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"Operators should identify needed changes, but a controlled plan remains subject to the organization''s approved review, authorization, revision, and document-control process. <b>D. Identify the update and route it through the approved document-control review.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 36 (print p. 133), VI.B.2.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"bokReference":"VI.B.2","options":["document control practices are suspended during operations.","standard operating procedures, failure modes, and effects analysis contradict each other.","root causes and corrective actions are applied to future versions.","Identify the update and route it through the approved document-control review."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":480,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":133,"sourceQuestion":36,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A dynamic control plan is a living document. How should operators handle a needed update when process conditions change?","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"Operators should identify needed changes, but a controlled plan remains subject to the organization''s approved review, authorization, revision, and document-control process. <b>D. Identify the update and route it through the approved document-control review.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 36 (print p. 133), VI.B.2.</span>"},"revision":"bd197acb1d40ccbebc0de75945e442d67f1611fc79aa5b8c81277082eec75fa8"},"cssgb:set-2:source-481:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"bokReference\":\"VI.B.2\",\"options\":[\"pictures, colors, and shapes.\",\"spreadsheets filled with numbers.\",\"illustrations, instructions, and procedures for implementation and maintenance.\",\"work instructions and user manuals.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":481,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":133,\"sourceQuestion\":37,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"Dynamic control planning supports control plans with:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"Illustrations, instructions, and procedures support control plans. <b>C. illustrations, instructions, and procedures for implementation and maintenance.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 37 (print p. 133), VI.B.2.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"bokReference":"VI.B.2","options":["pictures, colors, and shapes.","spreadsheets filled with numbers.","illustrations, instructions, and procedures for implementation and maintenance.","work instructions and user manuals."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":481,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":133,"sourceQuestion":37,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"Dynamic control planning supports control plans with:","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"Illustrations, instructions, and procedures support control plans. <b>C. illustrations, instructions, and procedures for implementation and maintenance.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 37 (print p. 133), VI.B.2.</span>"},"revision":"84964ea531deea72a05fc332cffd042c0d1978accacb629ee0c51acdc5554508"},"cssgb:set-2:source-482:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"bokReference\":\"VI.B.2\",\"options\":[\"Reprimand the operators, as adjustments are not permitted.\",\"Discard the documents, as the need for adjustments invalidates their suitability.\",\"Review the proposed adjustments to remove nonessential portions while inserting necessary components into new versions.\",\"Freely permit all operators to adjust documents at will.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":482,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":134,\"sourceQuestion\":38,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"How should the quality functional leadership respond if opera