stion\",\"stem\":\"What should training objectives be expressed as?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"Training objectives should be expressed as performance targets. There should be a clear mapping between the training activities and the desired performance. <b>D. Performance targets</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 43 (print p. 135), VI.B.3.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"bokReference":"VI.B.3","options":["Needs analysis","Business cases","Cost-and-benefit relationships","Performance targets"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":487,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":135,"sourceQuestion":43,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"What should training objectives be expressed as?","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"Training objectives should be expressed as performance targets. There should be a clear mapping between the training activities and the desired performance. <b>D. Performance targets</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 43 (print p. 135), VI.B.3.</span>"},"revision":"8e568334abe2fd52fe3d05ce39e5dfde1e22b7b98e95c4399d4eda092a8a3467"},"cssgb:set-2:source-488:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"VI.B.4\",\"options\":[\"First-party audit\",\"Second-party audit\",\"Third-party audit\",\"Fourth-party audit\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":488,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":135,\"sourceQuestion\":44,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"When an audit is conducted by local personnel on their own property, it is considered what type of audit?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"First-party audit (also described in ISO 19011:2018). An audit conducted by local personnel on their own property is considered a first-party audit. <b>A. First-party audit</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 44 (print p. 135), VI.B.4.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"bokReference":"VI.B.4","options":["First-party audit","Second-party audit","Third-party audit","Fourth-party audit"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":488,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":135,"sourceQuestion":44,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"When an audit is conducted by local personnel on their own property, it is considered what type of audit?","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"First-party audit (also described in ISO 19011:2018). An audit conducted by local personnel on their own property is considered a first-party audit. <b>A. First-party audit</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 44 (print p. 135), VI.B.4.</span>"},"revision":"f546908ef846c3189847394d0ee63064acca795444b338fe2b05e6c06db21ce7"},"cssgb:set-2:source-489:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"bokReference\":\"VI.B.4\",\"options\":[\"first-party audit.\",\"second-party audit.\",\"third-party audit.\",\"fourth-party audit.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":489,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":135,\"sourceQuestion\":45,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"When an independent registrar audits your organization, the audit type is called a:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"An audit performed by an independent registrar on an organization is a third-party audit. <b>C. third-party audit.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 45 (print p. 135), VI.B.4.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"bokReference":"VI.B.4","options":["first-party audit.","second-party audit.","third-party audit.","fourth-party audit."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":489,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":135,"sourceQuestion":45,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"When an independent registrar audits your organization, the audit type is called a:","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"An audit performed by an independent registrar on an organization is a third-party audit. <b>C. third-party audit.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 45 (print p. 135), VI.B.4.</span>"},"revision":"6f850e86d122f65abf5dcd26de9d3f11c04e1376618bfa66e8b22a7f05125fe8"},"cssgb:set-2:source-48:1f5xhgp":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"bokReference\":\"II.F.3\",\"options\":[\"force-field analysis.\",\"brainstorming.\",\"nominal group technique.\",\"process analysis.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":48,\"sourcePart\":\"Part B: Practice Exam\",\"sourcePrintPage\":159,\"sourceQuestion\":48,\"sourceSection\":\"II. Define Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book Practice Exam\",\"stem\":\"This idea-generation technique does not include verbal interactions and instead involves writing ideas first and then posting them for all to read. It is:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-define\",\"why\":\"The nominal group technique involves non-verbal interactions in which individual team members write down their brainstormed ideas first and then post them for the team to read. <b>C. nominal group technique.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 48 (print p. 159), II.F.3.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"bokReference":"II.F.3","options":["force-field analysis.","brainstorming.","nominal group technique.","process analysis."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":48,"sourcePart":"Part B: Practice Exam","sourcePrintPage":159,"sourceQuestion":48,"sourceSection":"II. Define Phase","sourceType":"Book Practice Exam","stem":"This idea-generation technique does not include verbal interactions and instead involves writing ideas first and then posting them for all to read. It is:","sub":"cssgb-define","why":"The nominal group technique involves non-verbal interactions in which individual team members write down their brainstormed ideas first and then post them for the team to read. <b>C. nominal group technique.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 48 (print p. 159), II.F.3.</span>"},"revision":"b25ec3a0871e82d9e3dc4d562fd40c39855b860d96c8e1fc15e14b3fd377f38b"},"cssgb:set-2:source-490:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"bokReference\":\"VI.B.4\",\"options\":[\"ensure that the root cause of the problem was identified correctly.\",\"sustain improvements by reinforcing those practices that contributed to improvement.\",\"verify that the operator work instructions are being followed as designed by the process.\",\"verify management commitment to the continual improvement of the operations.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":490,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":135,\"sourceQuestion\":46,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"A key factor in using ISO 19011 audits in Six Sigma is to:\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"In Six Sigma, a key factor of using ISO 19011 audits is to sustain improvements. This is done by reinforcing those practices that contributed to the improvement. <b>B. sustain improvements by reinforcing those practices that contributed to improvement.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 46 (print p. 135), VI.B.4.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"bokReference":"VI.B.4","options":["ensure that the root cause of the problem was identified correctly.","sustain improvements by reinforcing those practices that contributed to improvement.","verify that the operator work instructions are being followed as designed by the process.","verify management commitment to the continual improvement of the operations."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":490,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":135,"sourceQuestion":46,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A key factor in using ISO 19011 audits in Six Sigma is to:","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"In Six Sigma, a key factor of using ISO 19011 audits is to sustain improvements. This is done by reinforcing those practices that contributed to the improvement. <b>B. sustain improvements by reinforcing those practices that contributed to improvement.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 46 (print p. 135), VI.B.4.</span>"},"revision":"007f9c085b390706758342dc6fcd8cf1ac4d8c6e6466e62c26ccea18b7453c99"},"cssgb:set-2:source-491:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"bokReference\":\"VI.B.4\",\"options\":[\"FMEA.\",\"tollgate.\",\"Gemba.\",\"audit.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":491,\"sourcePart\":\"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK\",\"sourcePrintPage\":136,\"sourceQuestion\":47,\"sourceSection\":\"VI. Control Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book BoK Sample Question\",\"stem\":\"A type of quality assessment activity intended to reconcile the description of systems, processes, activities, and objective evidence with their actual outcomes is a(n):\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-control\",\"why\":\"An audit is a type of quality assessment activity intended to reconcile the description of systems, processes, activities, and objective evidence with their actual outcomes. <b>D. audit.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 47 (print p. 136), VI.B.4.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"bokReference":"VI.B.4","options":["FMEA.","tollgate.","Gemba.","audit."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/chapter6.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":491,"sourcePart":"Part A: Sample Questions by BoK","sourcePrintPage":136,"sourceQuestion":47,"sourceSection":"VI. Control Phase","sourceType":"Book BoK Sample Question","stem":"A type of quality assessment activity intended to reconcile the description of systems, processes, activities, and objective evidence with their actual outcomes is a(n):","sub":"cssgb-control","why":"An audit is a type of quality assessment activity intended to reconcile the description of systems, processes, activities, and objective evidence with their actual outcomes. <b>D. audit.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part A VI. Control Phase, Question 47 (print p. 136), VI.B.4.</span>"},"revision":"ad60807c3326d7a577cb2ff845eda1f262d6075ffbe4b3b145fa59ed4b7427f9"},"cssgb:set-2:source-492:uwm1ss":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"bokReference\":\"VI.B.4\",\"options\":[\"Second-party audits are conducted by external providers.\",\"Third-party audits are conducted by external providers.\",\"Third-party audits are conducted by a representative of a regulatory or accreditation body.\",\"Third-party audits are conducted by external providers as a condition of continued purchases or preservation of the business relationship.\"],\