obability of rejecting H₀ when H₀ is false. <b>C. the probability of rejecting H0 when it is false.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 86 (print p. 167), IV.B1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"bokReference":"IV.B1","options":["the critical value of the test.","Type II error.","the probability of rejecting H0 when it is false.","the probability of accepting H0 when it is true."],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":86,"sourcePart":"Part B: Practice Exam","sourcePrintPage":167,"sourceQuestion":86,"sourceSection":"IV. Analyze Phase","sourceType":"Book Practice Exam","stem":"In a statistical test, power is defined as:","sub":"cssgb-analyze","why":"Power is 1−β: the probability of rejecting H₀ when H₀ is false. <b>C. the probability of rejecting H0 when it is false.</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 86 (print p. 167), IV.B1.</span>"},"revision":"26279945ab43e5f01df764e7bc9b4b145b9b67cc851ecf11b23cfdf18d407cdb"},"cssgb:set-2:source-87:sebhe3":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"bokReference\":\"IV.C\",\"options\":[\"root cause.\",\"effect.\",\"dependent variable.\",\"critical value.\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":87,\"sourcePart\":\"Part B: Practice Exam\",\"sourcePrintPage\":167,\"sourceQuestion\":87,\"sourceSection\":\"IV. Analyze Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book Practice Exam\",\"stem\":\"A factor that caused a nonconformance and should be permanently eliminated through process improvement is a(n):\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-analyze\",\"why\":\"This question asks how to prevent reoccurrences, thus requiring a root cause. <b>A. root cause.</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 87 (print p. 167), IV.C.</span>\"}","co