t2.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":91,\"sourcePart\":\"Part B: Practice Exam\",\"sourcePrintPage\":168,\"sourceQuestion\":91,\"sourceSection\":\"III. Measure Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book Practice Exam\",\"stem\":\"There are three positions at an IT help desk, each of which handles trouble tickets from a different department. How many ways can the 12 IT employees be assigned to the help desk?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-measure\",\"why\":\"The three help-desk assignments are distinct positions, so order matters. P(12,3) = 12×11×10 = 1320. <b>D. 1320</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 91 (print p. 168), III.B.1.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"bokReference":"III.B.1","options":["4","12","220","1320"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":91,"sourcePart":"Part B: Practice Exam","sourcePrintPage":168,"sourceQuestion":91,"sourceSection":"III. Measure Phase","sourceType":"Book Practice Exam","stem":"There are three positions at an IT help desk, each of which handles trouble tickets from a different department. How many ways can the 12 IT employees be assigned to the help desk?","sub":"cssgb-measure","why":"The three help-desk assignments are distinct positions, so order matters. P(12,3) = 12×11×10 = 1320. <b>D. 1320</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 91 (print p. 168), III.B.1.</span>"},"revision":"31a2fe58ee545816df00079081e0d249b1f6796e18a0f68f5321d2745de298b9"},"cssgb:set-2:source-92:1up69ca":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"bokReference\":\"V.A.2\",\"chart\":{\"factorA\":\"A\",\"factorB\":\"B\",\"highLabel\":\"B high\",\"highLine\":[13,9.5],\"lowLabel\":\"B low\",\"lowLine\":[3,14],\"type\":\"two-level-interaction\"},\"options\":[\"Factor A low, Factor B low\",\"Factor A low, Factor B high\",\"Factor A high, Factor B low\",\"Factor A high, Factor B high\"],\"sourceEpubFile\":\"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml\",\"sourceGlobalQuestion\":92,\"sourcePart\":\"Part B: Practice Exam\",\"sourcePrintPage\":169,\"sourceQuestion\":92,\"sourceSection\":\"V. Improve Phase\",\"sourceType\":\"Book Practice Exam\",\"stem\":\"Using the interaction graph below, which factor settings will result in the largest mean response?\",\"sub\":\"cssgb-improve\",\"why\":\"The interaction plot reaches its largest fitted mean, 14, when Factor A is high and Factor B is low. <b>C. Factor A high, Factor B low</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 92 (print p. 169), V.A.2.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"bokReference":"V.A.2","chart":{"factorA":"A","factorB":"B","highLabel":"B high","highLine":[13,9.5],"lowLabel":"B low","lowLine":[3,14],"type":"two-level-interaction"},"options":["Factor A low, Factor B low","Factor A low, Factor B high","Factor A high, Factor B low","Factor A high, Factor B high"],"sourceEpubFile":"OEBPS/xhtml/part2.xhtml","sourceGlobalQuestion":92,"sourcePart":"Part B: Practice Exam","sourcePrintPage":169,"sourceQuestion":92,"sourceSection":"V. Improve Phase","sourceType":"Book Practice Exam","stem":"Using the interaction graph below, which factor settings will result in the largest mean response?","sub":"cssgb-improve","why":"The interaction plot reaches its largest fitted mean, 14, when Factor A is high and Factor B is low. <b>C. Factor A high, Factor B low</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The ASQ Certified Six Sigma Green Belt Study Guide (2024), Part B Practice Exam, Question 92 (print p. 169), V.A.2.</span>"},"revision":"f869c098afcf67b44e390d15356dbd81fa0168fe43a4b7ba877c75956b82d865"},"cssgb:set-2:source-93:1up69ca":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":1,\"bokReference\":\"V.C.1\",\"options\":[\"install racks to hold equipment.\",\"remove all obsolete equipment and materials.\",\"designate a place for every piece of equipm