urce: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 43; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["External escalation before the team discusses an issue internally","Performance feedback only at formal annual reviews","Restricting problem information to the project leader until a solution is selected","Open, candid communication without retaliation, timely internal issue awareness, and direct performance feedback"],"sourceAnswer":"E","sourceAssessment":"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI","sourceDocument":"The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook","sourceQuestion":43,"stem":"Which communication standard should an MBB establish for a project team?","sub":"mbb-org","why":"Healthy teams surface issues early, communicate without fear of retaliation, keep affected members informed, and provide direct performance feedback. <b>D. Open, candid communication without retaliation, timely internal issue awareness, and direct performance feedback</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 43; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>"},"revision":"28089c8b0e470cd116b865dd600211db4e52e899be4a794ed78e85675726022d"},"mbb:set-1:source-44":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"each level of management berates the level immediately below it until the lowest level is achieved and morale is significantly impaired\",\"suppliers suddenly ship excess inventory at the end of the month to meet revenue demands to achieve goals\",\"there is a sudden increase in employee attrition as bonus payouts are shifted from a gradient scale to an all-or-nothing scale\",\"there is a ripple effect on suppliers as customers change schedules or demand for products too frequently\"],\"sourceAnswer\":\"D\",\"sourceAssessment\":\"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI\",\"sourceDocument\":\"The Certified Six S