sis addresses uncertainty, and the project plan coordinates execution. <b>B. Project charter, risk analysis, and project plan</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 47; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>"},"revision":"fe061fb4eec7cc7b44e1b43a0c2f2c9a55e5623cebfa0d85b707b07bc44d8bc3"},"mbb:set-1:source-48":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"Model relevant cash flows, account for the time value of money when appropriate, and compare mutually exclusive alternatives consistently\",\"Use only ROI because discounting makes projects incomparable\",\"Use payback period alone and ignore cash flows after payback\",\"Select the project with the largest gross savings without considering investment or timing\"],\"sourceAnswer\":\"A\",\"sourceAssessment\":\"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI\",\"sourceDocument\":\"The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook\",\"sourceQuestion\":48,\"stem\":\"How should financially based project-selection methods be applied?\",\"sub\":\"mbb-portfolio\",\"why\":\"Sound financial comparison uses incremental cash flows and consistent timing assumptions; mutually exclusive alternatives must be evaluated on the same basis. <b>A. Model relevant cash flows, account for the time value of money when appropriate, and compare mutually exclusive alternatives consistently</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 48; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["Model relevant cash flows, account for the time value of money when appropriate, and compare mutually exclusive alternatives consistently","Use only ROI because discounting makes projects incomparable","Use payback period alone and ignore cash flows after payback","Select the project with the largest gross savings without considering investment or timin