 decomposition represents a time series with trend, seasonal, cyclical, and irregular components. Stationarity is a property of a series, not one of these components. <b>B. Trend, seasonal variation, cyclical variation, and irregular or residual variation</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 50; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["Stationarity, consumer effect, specification width, and autocorrelation","Trend, seasonal variation, cyclical variation, and irregular or residual variation","Mean shift, process capability, measurement bias, and seasonality","Trend, tolerance, control limits, and sampling error"],"sourceAnswer":"B","sourceAssessment":"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI","sourceDocument":"The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook","sourceQuestion":50,"stem":"Which set contains the standard components used to describe a time series?","sub":"mbb-analytics","why":"Classical decomposition represents a time series with trend, seasonal, cyclical, and irregular components. Stationarity is a property of a series, not one of these components. <b>B. Trend, seasonal variation, cyclical variation, and irregular or residual variation</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 50; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>"},"revision":"0df9e9f43ddcd4490ed5c0d969b825f264d881a50f57570cce38f41e03cd9f8f"},"mbb:set-1:source-51":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"The investigation has not yet established the causal path and final solution\",\"DMAIC projects are exempt from budget control\",\"Finance is not permitted to validate improvement benefits\",\"A project charter prohibits estimate refinement\"],\"sourceAnswer\":\"A\",\"sourceAssessment\":\"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI\",\"sourceDocument\":\"The 