aining catalog\",\"The organization’s strategic objectives and the workforce capabilities needed to execute them\",\"The preferences of individual project teams\",\"The prior year’s travel budget\"],\"sourceAnswer\":\"E\",\"sourceAssessment\":\"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI\",\"sourceDocument\":\"The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook\",\"sourceQuestion\":53,\"stem\":\"What should directly drive the human-resources strategic plan for a Lean Six Sigma deployment?\",\"sub\":\"mbb-enterprise\",\"why\":\"Workforce planning derives from enterprise strategy: HR identifies the roles, capacity, and competencies required to execute the organization’s objectives. <b>B. The organization’s strategic objectives and the workforce capabilities needed to execute them</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 53; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":1,"options":["The current training catalog","The organization’s strategic objectives and the workforce capabilities needed to execute them","The preferences of individual project teams","The prior year’s travel budget"],"sourceAnswer":"E","sourceAssessment":"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI","sourceDocument":"The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook","sourceQuestion":53,"stem":"What should directly drive the human-resources strategic plan for a Lean Six Sigma deployment?","sub":"mbb-enterprise","why":"Workforce planning derives from enterprise strategy: HR identifies the roles, capacity, and competencies required to execute the organization’s objectives. <b>B. The organization’s strategic objectives and the workforce capabilities needed to execute them</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 53; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>"},"revision":"5987cde745c4b87b12dcd60d8cf47dd6