 Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 56; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>"},"revision":"e25b918f9a3b6d1241f82f761fdeccfe5dee69894b81b15c5616c4dda639d371"},"mbb:set-1:source-57":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"Charge the cost back to the receiving business unit, or fund it from a central overhead budget\",\"Charge every learner personally, or record no cost\",\"Use only capital funding, or defer all training indefinitely\",\"Fund only external courses, or prohibit internal instruction\"],\"sourceAnswer\":\"A\",\"sourceAssessment\":\"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI\",\"sourceDocument\":\"The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook\",\"sourceQuestion\":57,\"stem\":\"Which pair describes two common organizational funding models for training?\",\"sub\":\"mbb-training\",\"why\":\"Training is commonly funded through a chargeback to the receiving unit or through a centralized overhead budget. The choice affects incentives, demand, and accountability. <b>A. Charge the cost back to the receiving business unit, or fund it from a central overhead budget</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 57; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["Charge the cost back to the receiving business unit, or fund it from a central overhead budget","Charge every learner personally, or record no cost","Use only capital funding, or defer all training indefinitely","Fund only external courses, or prohibit internal instruction"],"sourceAnswer":"A","sourceAssessment":"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI","sourceDocument":"The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook","sourceQuestion":57,"stem":"Which pair describes two common organizational funding models for training?","sub":"mbb-training","why":"Training is commonly funded through a chargeback to the receiving unit or through a centralized overhead budget. The choice affects incentives, demand, and accountability. <b>A. Charge the cost back to the receiving business unit, or fund it from a central overhead budget</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 57; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>"},"revision":"c6adaa832ecca4c5e7804e1d818188fb06bcb94ca8af1c973e5cd7bdaec47372"},"mbb:set-1:source-58":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"It guarantees motivation regardless of the work environment\",\"It automatically produces organizational results without practice or support\",\"It replaces the need for performance objectives and feedback\",\"It builds the capability and potential to achieve results but does not by itself guarantee them\"],\"sourceAnswer\":\"D\",\"sourceAssessment\":\"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI\",\"sourceDocument\":\"The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook\",\"sourceQuestion\":58,\"stem\":\"How does learning contribute to an individual’s performance?\",\"sub\":\"mbb-training\",\"why\":\"Learning develops capability. Performance still depends on practice, opportunity, motivation, resources, and reinforcement in the work environment. <b>D. It builds the capability and potential to achieve results but does not by itself guarantee them</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 58; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["It guarantees motivation regardless of the work environment","It automatically produces organizational results without practice or support","It replaces the need for performance objectives and feedback","It builds the capability and potential to achieve results but does not by itself guarantee them"],"sourceAnswer":"D","sourceAssessment":"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI","