 execution is not the conventional name used in this source framework. <b>B. Policy execution</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 59; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>"},"revision":"12f45107f970ec75a822c1fc719bc5e544554c1a7732872ee712cbfe80da2116"},"mbb:set-1:source-6":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":3,\"options\":[\"assigns a numerical rank to each data point for use with nonparametrical techniques\",\"removes the signal from the noise in time-series data\",\"stabilizes the ACF at the zero points\",\"permits the separation of a time series into trend and seasonal components\"],\"sourceAnswer\":\"D\",\"sourceAssessment\":\"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI\",\"sourceDocument\":\"The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook\",\"sourceQuestion\":6,\"stem\":\"The decomposition method\",\"sub\":\"mbb-analytics\",\"why\":\"Classical decomposition separates an observed time series into systematic components such as trend and seasonality plus residual variation. <b>D. permits the separation of a time series into trend and seasonal components</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 6; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":3,"options":["assigns a numerical rank to each data point for use with nonparametrical techniques","removes the signal from the noise in time-series data","stabilizes the ACF at the zero points","permits the separation of a time series into trend and seasonal components"],"sourceAnswer":"D","sourceAssessment":"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI","sourceDocument":"The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook","sourceQuestion":6,"stem":"The decomposition method","sub":"mbb-analytics","why":"Classical decomposition separates an observed time series into systematic components such as trend and seasonality p