uld proceed?","sub":"mbb-coaching","why":"The sponsor or champion owns the business decision at a tollgate. The MBB may coach and test technical rigor but does not replace sponsor accountability. <b>C. The project sponsor or champion</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 63; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>"},"revision":"f98881a4dff6ad96e322e813c55792d1240cdbf55414c0d545ca5e283e277591"},"mbb:set-1:source-64":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":2,\"options\":[\"Collecting customer comments without linking them to process measures\",\"Rotating marketing and operations managers regardless of business need\",\"Regular senior-management review with visible ownership, accountability, and action follow-through\",\"Reporting only favorable measures at the annual strategy meeting\"],\"sourceAnswer\":\"C\",\"sourceAssessment\":\"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI\",\"sourceDocument\":\"The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook\",\"sourceQuestion\":64,\"stem\":\"Which governance mechanism best sustains an integrated voice-of-the-customer and voice-of-the-process system?\",\"sub\":\"mbb-org\",\"why\":\"Regular executive review connects customer and process evidence to decisions, owners, and follow-through. Collection alone does not create an integrated management system. <b>C. Regular senior-management review with visible ownership, accountability, and action follow-through</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 64; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":2,"options":["Collecting customer comments without linking them to process measures","Rotating marketing and operations managers regardless of business need","Regular senior-management review with visible ownership, accountability, and action follow-through","Reporting only favorable measures at