: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 83; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>"},"revision":"5f40e48ce84c433c043b32a1c068e993b48e0ba9bde32d46f1889b69970637f2"},"mbb:set-1:source-84":{"canonicalContent":"{\"answer\":0,\"options\":[\"time, cost, quality, scope\",\"cost of quality, resources, customer relationships, budget\",\"scope, cost of quality, on-time delivery, customer relationships\",\"cost, time, budget, scope\"],\"sourceAnswer\":\"A\",\"sourceAssessment\":\"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI\",\"sourceDocument\":\"The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook\",\"sourceQuestion\":84,\"stem\":\"According to Williams''s balanced quadrant approach, managing a project requires balancing\",\"sub\":\"mbb-portfolio\",\"why\":\"The balanced project constraints are time, cost, quality, and scope; changing one commonly forces tradeoffs in one or more of the others. <b>A. time, cost, quality, scope</b> <span class=\\\"tb-source-ref\\\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 84; normalized for four-choice delivery.</span>\"}","content":{"answer":0,"options":["time, cost, quality, scope","cost of quality, resources, customer relationships, budget","scope, cost of quality, on-time delivery, customer relationships","cost, time, budget, scope"],"sourceAnswer":"A","sourceAssessment":"Simulated Examination Questions for Parts I–VI","sourceDocument":"The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook","sourceQuestion":84,"stem":"According to Williams''s balanced quadrant approach, managing a project requires balancing","sub":"mbb-portfolio","why":"The balanced project constraints are time, cost, quality, and scope; changing one commonly forces tradeoffs in one or more of the others. <b>A. time, cost, quality, scope</b> <span class=\"tb-source-ref\">Source: The Certified Six Sigma Master Black Belt Handbook, simulated examination, Question 84; normalized 